      "lineAnnotations": {
        "0": {"synopsis":"The unused lower half of the EXTH chip: 4K of $FF. The chip runs at $E000-$FFFF in the EXT\npage, so this half would be $E000-$EFFF; nothing in the ROM jumps or reads there, and its\ncode starts at $1000 ($F000)."},
        "4096": {"synopsis":"The boot's RAM set-up, entered from the SYS low chip's RESET_EXTH_INIT with EXT in page 3\n(after a cold start A' holds the U3 test result).\n1. Port 02h = $D0 (EXT in page 3, the video RAM in page 2, U0 in page 0); after a cold start\n   ($0B21 = 0) keeps A' in $0B1B.\n2. Copies 32 glyphs (320 bytes from $1B6B) to RAM $0740 for codes $80-$9F, then the next\n   glyph 64 times for codes $A0-$DF.\n3. Copies the two system call channel tables ($1B0E) to $0B00-$0B0F, the restart code\n   ($1B1E) to $0030-$003F and the system call's RAM part ($1B2E) to $0B23-$0B48.\n4. $0B10 = $FC (the interrupt calls devices 0 and 1 only), $0B13 = $80 (port 06h's copy),\n   $0B1F = $01, $0B17 = $0F10.\n5. Scans the four expansion slots by their 2-bit codes in port 5Ah: code 3 is a card whose\n   ROM starts with \"MOPS\" and names itself at $C004, codes 0, 1 and 2 are the RS232, VGB and\n   DISK cards named in this chip ($1B5C, $1B58, $1B62). Each name goes to the slot's 48-byte\n   record at $0040, $0070, $00A0 or $00D0; an empty slot's record starts with $FF.\n6. The first RS232 slot becomes entry 7 of both channel tables ($0B07, $0B0F) and the\n   default card in $0B1C ($FF: none).\n7. Numbers cards of the same name (byte 7 of the record: 0, 1, ...), sets the RS232 line up\n   (BAUD_DEFAULT: RS232_SET_BAUD with A = 4) and calls each other card's initialisation (the\n   word at $C00B in its ROM) with IX = its record.\n8. Returns to the SYS low chip's BOOT_IO_INIT through $FFF0.","comment":"EXT in page 3, the video RAM in page 2"},
        "4100": {"comment":"A warm start ($0B21 not 0)?"},
        "4106": {"comment":"The U3 test result from A'"},
        "4107": {"comment":"kept in $0B1B after a cold start"},
        "4110": {"synopsis":"Copies the 32 glyphs of codes $80-$9F to RAM $0740, then the next glyph 64 times for codes\n$A0-$DF.","comment":"The glyphs: 10 bytes each"},
        "4113": {"comment":"The RAM character set"},
        "4116": {"comment":"32 glyphs for codes $80-$9F"},
        "4121": {"comment":"Codes $A0-$DF: 64 copies of one glyph"},
        "4123": {"synopsis":"Copies the same 10-byte glyph once more, for the next code of $A0-$DF.","comment":"The same glyph each time"},
        "4124": {"comment":"One glyph"},
        "4129": {"comment":"64 done?"},
        "4132": {"comment":"The channel tables, from $1B0E"},
        "4135": {"comment":"to $0B00-$0B0F"},
        "4142": {"comment":"The restart code, from $1B1E"},
        "4145": {"comment":"to $0030-$003F (RST $30, the interrupt)"},
        "4149": {"comment":"The system call's RAM part, from $1B2E"},
        "4152": {"comment":"38 bytes to $0B23-$0B48"},
        "4156": {"comment":"Devices 0 and 1 only in the interrupt"},
        "4161": {"comment":"Port 06h's copy"},
        "4166": {"comment":"$01"},
        "4167": {"comment":"$0B1F = $01"},
        "4170": {"comment":"$0F10"},
        "4173": {"comment":"into $0B17"},
        "4176": {"comment":"2 bits per slot: the card codes"},
        "4178": {"comment":"B = 4 slots, C = the 2-bit mask"},
        "4181": {"comment":"The first slot record"},
        "4184": {"synopsis":"For each slot: selects it in port 03h bits 7-6 and puts the card's name in its record: from\nthe card's ROM for code 3, from this chip's names for codes 0-2.","comment":"D = the codes still to look at"},
        "4185": {"comment":"The slot number, 4 - B"},
        "4188": {"comment":"into bits 7-6"},
        "4190": {"comment":"Select the slot's card window"},
        "4193": {"comment":"This slot's code"},
        "4194": {"comment":"Code 3: a card with a ROM?"},
        "4196": {"comment":"The record address, for the copy"},
        "4197": {"comment":"The alternate set for the copy"},
        "4200": {"comment":"Code 0: \"RS232\""},
        "4203": {"comment":"Code 0?"},
        "4206": {"comment":"Code 1: \"VGB\""},
        "4209": {"comment":"Code 1?"},
        "4212": {"comment":"Code 2: \"DISK\""},
        "4217": {"synopsis":"Code 3: does the card's ROM at $C000 start with \"MOPS\"?","comment":"The card's window"},
        "4220": {"comment":"\"MOPS\""},
        "4223": {"comment":"4 characters"},
        "4225": {"synopsis":"Compares the next character of \"MOPS\" with the card's ROM."},
        "4226": {"comment":"Not the signature?"},
        "4231": {"comment":"All four?"},
        "4233": {"synopsis":"Copies the name at HL (a length byte, then the text) to the slot's record. For a card with a\nROM the name follows \"MOPS\", at $C004.","comment":"The length"},
        "4234": {"comment":"and the length byte itself"},
        "4237": {"comment":"The record"},
        "4238": {"comment":"The name into the record"},
        "4242": {"synopsis":"No card the ROM knows: the record starts with $FF.","comment":"The record"},
        "4243": {"comment":"$FF: no card here"},
        "4245": {"synopsis":"Moves to the next slot's code and record.","comment":"Back to the scan registers"},
        "4246": {"comment":"The next slot's code into bits 1-0"},
        "4249": {"comment":"48 bytes a record"},
        "4253": {"comment":"All four slots?"},
        "4255": {"comment":"Again over the four codes"},
        "4257": {"synopsis":"Looks for the first slot with code 0, the RS232 card: it becomes entry 7 of both channel\ntables (the card device 6 uses) and the default card in $0B1C.","comment":"D = the codes still to look at"},
        "4258": {"comment":"Code 0, RS232?"},
        "4261": {"comment":"The slot number, 4 - B"},
        "4264": {"comment":"Entry 7 of the $0B00 table"},
        "4267": {"comment":"and of the $0B08 table"},
        "4272": {"synopsis":"Moves to the next slot's code; after four, no RS232 card: $FF.","comment":"The next code into bits 1-0"},
        "4275": {"comment":"All four?"},
        "4277": {"comment":"No RS232 card"},
        "4279": {"synopsis":"Keeps the default card's slot in $0B1C (the value the error path puts back into a channel\nentry), then clears byte 7 of the four records.","comment":"The default card, or $FF"},
        "4282": {"comment":"Byte 7 of the first record"},
        "4285": {"comment":"48 bytes a record"},
        "4288": {"comment":"Four records"},
        "4291": {"synopsis":"Clears byte 7 of the next record (the card's number among cards of the same name)."},
        "4295": {"comment":"DE = $0040, the first record"},
        "4297": {"comment":"HL = $0070, the next one"},
        "4303": {"synopsis":"Compares the record at IY with an earlier one at IX (DE): the same name counts IY's card\nnumber (byte 7) up, so that cards of one name are numbered 0, 1, ...","comment":"IY = the later record"},
        "4306": {"comment":"The earlier record's length"},
        "4307": {"comment":"and its length byte"},
        "4308": {"synopsis":"Compares the next byte of the two names."},
        "4309": {"comment":"Another name?"},
        "4314": {"comment":"The whole name?"},
        "4316": {"comment":"The same name: the next number"},
        "4319": {"synopsis":"Moves IY to the next record; past the last ($0100) moves IX on and starts IY just after it,\nuntil IX is the last record."},
        "4322": {"comment":"48 bytes a record"},
        "4326": {"comment":"Past the last record ($0100)?"},
        "4330": {"comment":"The next earlier record"},
        "4334": {"comment":"Was IX the last one?"},
        "4338": {"comment":"IX moves on"},
        "4341": {"comment":"IY starts just after it"},
        "4342": {"synopsis":"Takes IX into DE as the name to compare with and goes on comparing."},
        "4347": {"synopsis":"Sets the RS232 line up (BAUD_DEFAULT: RS232_SET_BAUD with A = 4), then calls the\ninitialisation routine of each card with a code of 1-3 (the word at $C00B in its ROM) with\nIX = its record; then returns to the SYS low chip's BOOT_IO_INIT through $FFF0.","comment":"U2 in page 2 again"},
        "4351": {"comment":"BAUD_DEFAULT: RS232_SET_BAUD with A = 4"},
        "4354": {"comment":"The first slot record"},
        "4358": {"comment":"Four slots"},
        "4360": {"comment":"The card codes"},
        "4362": {"synopsis":"For the next slot: selects its card window and calls the card's initialisation unless the\nslot is empty or holds the RS232 card (code 0).","comment":"C = the codes still to look at"},
        "4363": {"comment":"The slot number, 4 - B"},
        "4366": {"comment":"into bits 7-6"},
        "4368": {"comment":"Select the slot's card window"},
        "4370": {"comment":"An empty slot ($FF)?"},
        "4376": {"comment":"Code 0, the RS232 card?"},
        "4381": {"comment":"The card ROM's initialisation"},
        "4385": {"comment":"IX = the record, for the card"},
        "4387": {"comment":"Call it (JP (HL))"},
        "4393": {"comment":"Port 02h back, the card may change it"},
        "4397": {"synopsis":"Moves to the next record and slot code.","comment":"48 bytes a record"},
        "4402": {"comment":"The next slot's code into bits 1-0"},
        "4405": {"comment":"All four?"},
        "4407": {"comment":"The SYS low chip's BOOT_IO_INIT"},
        "4410": {"comment":"through $FFF0, SYS in page 3"},
        "4413": {"synopsis":"RESET's RAM check, entered from the SYS low chip's RESET_TO_EXTH with EXT in page 3 and A =\nthe port 02h value to go back with. Compares the system call's RAM part at $0B23 (30 bytes)\nwith its original at $1B2E: when it is intact and $0B21 is 0, $0B21 becomes $FF (the SYS low\nchip's RESET_HW_INIT then makes a warm start); a difference, or $0B21 already set, leaves\n$0B21 = 0 (a cold start). Then restores port 02h from A and jumps to RESET_RESUME in the SYS\nlow chip's page-0 copy ($023A).\nEntry: A = the port 02h value for the return.","comment":"Keep the port 02h value"},
        "4414": {"comment":"EXT in page 3, the video RAM in page 2"},
        "4418": {"comment":"The original, at $1B2E"},
        "4421": {"comment":"The RAM copy"},
        "4424": {"comment":"30 bytes"},
        "4427": {"synopsis":"Compares the next byte of the RAM copy with the original."},
        "4429": {"comment":"Compare with the RAM byte"},
        "4431": {"comment":"Changed: a cold start"},
        "4433": {"comment":"More bytes?"},
        "4436": {"comment":"Intact: was $0B21 0?"},
        "4440": {"comment":"Then $FF: a warm start"},
        "4444": {"synopsis":"A cold start: $0B21 = 0."},
        "4445": {"synopsis":"Stores the verdict in $0B21, restores port 02h and goes back to the SYS low chip's\nRESET_RESUME.","comment":"$FF warm, 0 cold"},
        "4448": {"comment":"The port 02h value"},
        "4449": {"comment":"back as it was"},
        "4451": {"comment":"The SYS low chip's RESET_RESUME, at $023A"},
        "4454": {"synopsis":"The system call for a channel entry with bit 7 set, reached from the SYS low chip's\nSC_TEST_CARD through $FFF0 (HL = $F166): the entry names a card. The SYS low chip has\ncleared bit 7, so A is the slot; goes on at CARD_CALL with HL = the entry.\nEntry: B = the entry (0-6), DE = the RAM table ($0B00 or $0B08), A = the entry's byte\nwithout bit 7, C = the function, A' = the code; the caller's DE and BC on the stack.","comment":"The entry"},
        "4457": {"comment":"in the RAM table"},
        "4460": {"synopsis":"Device 6's system call, reached from the SYS low chip's SC_TEST_DEV6 through $FFF0 (HL =\n$F16C): the card is the one in entry 7 of the RAM table, then as for CARD_SYSCALL.\nEntry: DE = the RAM table ($0B00 or $0B08), C = the function, A' = the code; the caller's DE\nand BC on the stack.","comment":"Entry 7: the card for device 6"},
        "4464": {"comment":"Its slot"},
        "4465": {"synopsis":"Calls function C of the card in slot A:\n1. A slot of 4 or more, or an empty slot (record byte 0 = $FF), puts the default card $0B1C\n   back into the entry and fails with $FE.\n2. Selects the slot (port 03h and its copy $0B11). A card named \"RS232\" uses this chip's\n   function list RS232_FUNCS; any other card the list at $C00D in its ROM (a count, then the\n   words). A function past the count fails with $FF.\n3. Calls the function (through CALL_HL, JP (HL)) with IX = the slot's record + 8 (the bytes\n   after the slot's name and number), A = the code and the caller's BC and DE, then returns\n   its result to the SYS low chip's SC_RESULT through $FFF0.\nEntry: A = the slot (0-3; $FF, no card, fails), HL = the channel entry, C = the function, A'\n= the code.","comment":"Slot 0-3?"},
        "4469": {"comment":"Keep B, C and DE"},
        "4470": {"comment":"The first slot record"},
        "4473": {"comment":"48 bytes a record"},
        "4476": {"comment":"B = the slot"},
        "4477": {"comment":"into bits 7-6"},
        "4479": {"comment":"Port 03h's copy"},
        "4482": {"comment":"Select the card's window"},
        "4484": {"comment":"Slot 0?"},
        "4488": {"synopsis":"Steps to the slot's record, 48 bytes at a time."},
        "4491": {"synopsis":"Checks the slot's record: an empty slot fails; then compares its name with \"RS232\".","comment":"An empty slot ($FF)?"},
        "4495": {"comment":"The name's length"},
        "4496": {"comment":"Its text"},
        "4497": {"comment":"\"RS232\" (after its length byte)"},
        "4500": {"synopsis":"Compares the next character of the card's name with \"RS232\"."},
        "4502": {"comment":"Compare with the record"},
        "4504": {"comment":"Another name?"},
        "4506": {"comment":"The whole name?"},
        "4509": {"comment":"The caller's B, C and DE"},
        "4510": {"comment":"The RS232 card: this chip's own functions"},
        "4515": {"synopsis":"Any other card: its function list is at $C00D in its ROM.","comment":"Back to the caller's registers"},
        "4516": {"comment":"The card ROM's function list"},
        "4519": {"synopsis":"Picks function C's word from the list at HL (a count, then the words), and IX = the slot's\nrecord + 8.","comment":"The count"},
        "4521": {"comment":"Is the function in the list?"},
        "4522": {"comment":"No: $FF at $11E0"},
        "4524": {"comment":"The words"},
        "4526": {"comment":"C x 2"},
        "4531": {"comment":"The function's address"},
        "4535": {"comment":"The selected slot"},
        "4538": {"comment":"from bits 7-6 to bits 1-0"},
        "4542": {"comment":"Slot 0's card RAM"},
        "4546": {"comment":"48 bytes a record"},
        "4552": {"synopsis":"Steps IX to the slot's card RAM."},
        "4556": {"synopsis":"Calls the card's function with A = the code and the caller's DE and BC.","comment":"A = the code (from A')"},
        "4557": {"comment":"The caller's DE"},
        "4558": {"comment":"and BC"},
        "4559": {"comment":"Call the function (JP (HL))"},
        "4562": {"synopsis":"Returns A, the result, to the SYS low chip's SC_RESULT through $FFF0 (SYS in page 3).","comment":"The SYS low chip's SC_RESULT"},
        "4565": {"comment":"through $FFF0"},
        "4568": {"synopsis":"An empty slot: back to the registers that address the entry."},
        "4569": {"synopsis":"Puts the default card ($0B1C) back into the entry and fails with $FE (a bad entry); $11E0,\nhidden in the next instruction, fails with $FF (no such function).","comment":"The default card"},
        "4572": {"comment":"back into the entry"},
        "4573": {"comment":"$FE: a bad entry"},
        "4575": {"comment":"Hides $11E0: ld a,$FF (no such function)"},
        "4578": {"comment":"Drop the caller's DE"},
        "4580": {"comment":"and return the error"},
        "4582": {"synopsis":"The system call's error path, reached from the SYS low chip's SC_RESULT through $FFF0 with A\n= the code: puts the channel entry the code used back to its default (from $1B0E for the\n$0B00 table, $1B16 for $0B08). An entry holding device 6 also resets entry 7 (the card\ndevice 6 uses) to the default card $0B1C; an entry holding a card (bit 7 set) and entry 7\nitself are left as they are. Returns to the SYS low chip's SC_ERR_RETURN through $FFF0.\nEntry: A = the system call code.","comment":"Bit 7 of the code: which table?"},
        "4583": {"comment":"The $0B00 table"},
        "4586": {"comment":"and its defaults"},
        "4589": {"comment":"Its entry 7"},
        "4593": {"comment":"Bit 7 set: $0B00"},
        "4595": {"comment":"The $0B08 table"},
        "4598": {"comment":"and its defaults"},
        "4601": {"comment":"Its entry 7"},
        "4605": {"synopsis":"Takes the entry (bits 6-4 of the code) and puts its default back, unless it is entry 7 or\nholds a card.","comment":"Bits 6-4 to bits 2-0"},
        "4610": {"comment":"Entry 7?"},
        "4614": {"comment":"The entry"},
        "4617": {"comment":"in the table"},
        "4619": {"comment":"and in the defaults"},
        "4621": {"comment":"What the entry holds now"},
        "4622": {"comment":"Device 6?"},
        "4624": {"comment":"Then entry 7 = the default card"},
        "4627": {"comment":"A card (bit 7)? Left alone"},
        "4630": {"comment":"The default"},
        "4631": {"comment":"back into the entry"},
        "4632": {"synopsis":"Returns to the SYS low chip's SC_ERR_RETURN through $FFF0.","comment":"The SYS low chip's SC_ERR_RETURN"},
        "4635": {"comment":"through $FFF0"},
        "4638": {"synopsis":"Puts the default card ($0B1C) into entry 7 of the table (IX); keeps AF."},
        "4639": {"comment":"The default card"},
        "4642": {"comment":"into entry 7"},
        "4647": {"synopsis":"Serves the cards' interrupts, reached from the SYS low chip's INT_EXTH_CARDS through $FFF0\n(from INT_POLL_DEVS for the bits 4-7 of $0B10, and from INT_SERVICE for the slots signalling\nin port 59h): for each slot whose bit in C is 0, selects its card window and calls function\n0 of its ROM's list (the word at $C00E); then restores port 03h from $0B11 and returns to\nthe SYS address on the stack through $FFF0.\nEntry: C bits 3-0 = the slots, 0 = serve; the return address in SYS on the stack.","comment":"Four slots"},
        "4649": {"synopsis":"Takes the next slot's bit; a 0 calls its card's function 0.","comment":"The next slot's bit"},
        "4651": {"comment":"1: nothing to serve"},
        "4654": {"comment":"The slot number, 4 - B"},
        "4657": {"comment":"into bits 7-6"},
        "4659": {"comment":"Select the slot's card window"},
        "4661": {"comment":"Function 0 of the card ROM's list"},
        "4664": {"comment":"Call it (JP (HL))"},
        "4667": {"comment":"Port 02h back, the card may change it"},
        "4672": {"synopsis":"Moves to the next slot; after four, restores port 03h and returns to SYS."},
        "4674": {"comment":"The selected slot as before"},
        "4679": {"comment":"The return address in SYS"},
        "4680": {"comment":"through $FFF0, SYS in page 3"},
        "4683": {"synopsis":"Writes a block one character at a time through a character function, for devices whose block\nfunction has no faster way (the RS232 card, a cassette data file). Each byte goes to the\nfunction in C; a byte above the top of RAM ($0B19) fails with $FA, and a nonzero result ends\nthe loop with it.\nEntry: HL = the character function, DE = the block, BC = its length (not 0).\nExit: A = 0 when all were written, otherwise the error.","comment":"HL = the block, DE = the function"},
        "4684": {"synopsis":"Sends the next byte: checks that it is below the top of RAM, calls the function with C = the\nbyte and stops on an error."},
        "4687": {"comment":"The address, for the check"},
        "4688": {"comment":"The function"},
        "4689": {"comment":"DE = the address"},
        "4690": {"comment":"The top of RAM"},
        "4694": {"comment":"Beyond it?"},
        "4696": {"comment":"$FA: above the top of RAM"},
        "4700": {"comment":"Beyond: fail"},
        "4701": {"comment":"C = the byte"},
        "4702": {"comment":"HL = the function"},
        "4703": {"comment":"Write it (JP (HL))"},
        "4709": {"comment":"An error?"},
        "4711": {"comment":"The next byte; BC counts down"},
        "4713": {"comment":"All written?"},
        "4716": {"synopsis":"Reads a block one character at a time through a character function (the RS232 card, a\ncassette data file). Each byte the function returns in C goes to DE; a destination above the\ntop of RAM ($0B19) fails with $FA, and a nonzero result ends the loop with it.\nEntry: HL = the character function, DE = the destination, BC = the length (not 0).\nExit: A = 0 when all were read, otherwise the error."},
        "4719": {"comment":"The function"},
        "4720": {"comment":"The destination"},
        "4721": {"comment":"The top of RAM"},
        "4725": {"comment":"Beyond it?"},
        "4727": {"comment":"$FA: above the top of RAM"},
        "4731": {"comment":"Beyond: fail"},
        "4732": {"comment":"Read one (JP (HL))"},
        "4735": {"comment":"Keep the result"},
        "4736": {"comment":"A = the byte"},
        "4740": {"comment":"The result"},
        "4741": {"comment":"An error?"},
        "4743": {"comment":"The byte"},
        "4744": {"comment":"into the block"},
        "4746": {"comment":"HL = the destination"},
        "4747": {"comment":"The next one; BC counts down"},
        "4750": {"comment":"All read?"},
        "4753": {"synopsis":"RS232_FUNCS: the RS232 card's function list, used by CARD_CALL for a card named \"RS232\" in\nplace of a card ROM's list: a count of 5, then the words of functions 0-4: RS232_F0 (the\ninterrupt's call does nothing), RS232_CHAR, RS232_BLOCK, RS232_INIT (open: sets the line up)\nand RS232_F4_OK (close does nothing)."},
        "4764": {"synopsis":"Sets the RS232 line's speed index $0B69 to A and its format byte $0B6A to $EE, then sets the\nline up (falls into RS232_INIT). The boot reaches it through BAUD_DEFAULT with A = 4.\nEntry: A = the speed index (0-8, RS232_BAUD_TABLE).","comment":"The speed index"},
        "4767": {"comment":"The format byte"},
        "4772": {"synopsis":"Sets the RS232 line up (also the card's function 3, open):\n1. Clears port 06h bits 5-2 (the sound's volume; copy $0B13).\n2. Programs the sound generator's divider (port 04h, port 05h bits 3-0 with bit 4 set; copy\n   $0B12) with the word of RS232_BAUD_TABLE picked by $0B69 (capped at 8): which the card is\n   clocked from.\n3. For each slot whose code in port 5Ah is 0 (an RS232 card) writes 0, 0, 0, $40 and then\n   the mode byte ($0B6A AND $B4, OR $4A) to the card's port $x1 (slot n: $11 + 16n). What\n   these bytes set in the card is not shown by this ROM.\n4. Clears $0B71, which SND_START and the tape code set when they reprogram the sound\n   generator, so that the next character call sets the line up again.\nChanges: AF, DE."},
        "4774": {"comment":"Port 06h's copy"},
        "4777": {"comment":"Bits 5-2 off: no volume"},
        "4784": {"comment":"The speed index"},
        "4787": {"comment":"Above 8?"},
        "4791": {"comment":"At most 8"},
        "4793": {"synopsis":"Takes the speed's divider from RS232_BAUD_TABLE and writes it to the sound generator.","comment":"Index x 2"},
        "4797": {"comment":"RS232_BAUD_TABLE"},
        "4801": {"comment":"The divider"},
        "4804": {"comment":"Its high bits 3-0"},
        "4807": {"comment":"with bit 4: the oscillator on"},
        "4810": {"comment":"Port 05h's copy"},
        "4813": {"comment":"keeping bits 7-6 (the motors)"},
        "4819": {"comment":"The divider high bits"},
        "4821": {"comment":"and its low byte"},
        "4824": {"comment":"The format byte"},
        "4827": {"comment":"into the mode byte"},
        "4831": {"comment":"H = the mode"},
        "4832": {"comment":"Four slots, from port $11"},
        "4835": {"comment":"D = $40, E = the code mask"},
        "4838": {"comment":"The card codes"},
        "4840": {"synopsis":"For each slot with code 0 (an RS232 card) writes the reset and mode bytes to its port $x1.","comment":"L = the codes still to look at"},
        "4841": {"comment":"Code 0, RS232?"},
        "4844": {"comment":"0 three times"},
        "4850": {"comment":"$40"},
        "4852": {"comment":"then the mode"},
        "4854": {"synopsis":"Moves to the next slot's port ($10 on) and code; after four clears $0B71.","comment":"The next slot's port"},
        "4858": {"comment":"The next code into bits 1-0"},
        "4861": {"comment":"All four?"},
        "4863": {"comment":"Set up: no need to repeat it"},
        "4869": {"synopsis":"The RS232 card's function 0, called from the interrupt: returns at once (the RET of\nRS232_INIT)."},
        "4870": {"synopsis":"Waits while a sound plays: the sound generator is the serial clock. A break request returns\n$F5.","comment":"A break?"},
        "4874": {"synopsis":"Waits until no sound plays ($0B14 = 0), then gives the selected card's status port.\nEntry: C = the character to send.\nExit: carry set, A = 0, H = the character, C = the port $x1 of the slot in $0B11; or NC with\nA = $F5 on a break.","comment":"A sound playing?"},
        "4880": {"comment":"H = the character"},
        "4881": {"comment":"The selected slot"},
        "4884": {"comment":"bits 7-6 to 5-4"},
        "4888": {"comment":"Port $x1 of the slot"},
        "4891": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "4892": {"comment":"carry: carry on"},
        "4894": {"comment":"Never reached"},
        "4895": {"synopsis":"Waits until the card's status port shows bits 7 and 0 both set, checking for a break.\nExit: carry set when ready; NC with A = $F5 on a break.","comment":"Wait for the sound, take the port"},
        "4898": {"comment":"A break?"},
        "4899": {"synopsis":"Reads the status until bits 7 and 0 are both set.","comment":"The status"},
        "4903": {"comment":"Both set?"},
        "4905": {"comment":"carry: ready"},
        "4906": {"comment":"Ready"},
        "4907": {"comment":"A break?"},
        "4910": {"comment":"No: again"},
        "4913": {"synopsis":"Is a break requested ($0B16 not 0)? Exit: Z and NC when not; NZ, NC and A = $F5 when one is.","comment":"The break flag"},
        "4918": {"comment":"$F5: a break"},
        "4921": {"synopsis":"The RS232 card's function 1, the character function: the input side (code with bit 7 set)\nreads one (RS232_GET), the output side writes one (RS232_PUT, falls into it).\nEntry: A = the code; C = the character to write.","comment":"The input side?"},
        "4924": {"synopsis":"Sends the character in C on the selected RS232 card: waits until it is ready, sets the line\nup again if the sound generator was reprogrammed ($0B71), writes $05 to the command port,\nwaits for bit 0 of the status, then writes the character to the data port $x0.\nExit: A = 0, or $F5 on a break.","comment":"Ready, port in C, character in H"},
        "4927": {"comment":"A break"},
        "4928": {"comment":"Sound generator reprogrammed?"},
        "4932": {"comment":"Then set the line up again"},
        "4935": {"comment":"$05 to the command port"},
        "4939": {"synopsis":"Waits for bit 0 of the status, checking for a break, then sends the character.","comment":"A break?"},
        "4943": {"comment":"The status"},
        "4945": {"comment":"Bit 0: ready?"},
        "4948": {"comment":"The data port $x0"},
        "4949": {"comment":"The character"},
        "4951": {"synopsis":"Returns A = 0: the end of RS232_PUT, and the RS232 card's function 4 (close), which does\nnothing."},
        "4953": {"synopsis":"Reads a character from the selected RS232 card: waits until no sound plays, sets the line up\nagain if needed ($0B71), then takes a character at once if status bit 1 says one is there;\notherwise waits for it (RS_GET_WAIT).\nExit: A = 0 and C = the character; $F5 on a break; $F2-$F4 for a line error (RS_GET_DONE).","comment":"Wait for the sound, take the port"},
        "4956": {"comment":"A break"},
        "4957": {"comment":"Sound generator reprogrammed?"},
        "4961": {"comment":"Then set the line up again"},
        "4964": {"comment":"The status"},
        "4966": {"comment":"Bit 1: a character there?"},
        "4970": {"comment":"The data port $x0"},
        "4971": {"comment":"The character"},
        "4973": {"comment":"into C"},
        "4976": {"synopsis":"Waits for a character with interrupts off: selects keyboard row 7 (port 03h, keeping the\nslot) and writes $25 to the command port, then polls the status, giving up with $F5 (a\nbreak) when both keys read by port 58h bits 4-3 are held (bit 3 of $0B62 is set too)."},
        "4977": {"comment":"The selected slot"},
        "4982": {"comment":"with keyboard row 7"},
        "4986": {"comment":"$25 to the command port"},
        "4990": {"synopsis":"Are both keys of row 7 bits 4-3 held? Then a break.","comment":"Keyboard row 7"},
        "4992": {"comment":"Bits 4-3: both keys down?"},
        "4996": {"comment":"Bit 3 of $0B62"},
        "5001": {"comment":"$F5: a break"},
        "5005": {"synopsis":"Polls status bit 1; when a character is there writes $05 to the command port, reads the\nstatus and the character, and checks the status's error bits 5-3: bit 3 gives $F4, bit 4\n$F2, bit 5 $F3, each after $11 to the command port.","comment":"The status"},
        "5007": {"comment":"Bit 1: a character?"},
        "5011": {"comment":"$05 to the command port"},
        "5015": {"comment":"The status again"},
        "5017": {"comment":"The data port $x0"},
        "5018": {"comment":"H = the character"},
        "5021": {"comment":"Error bits 5-3?"},
        "5026": {"comment":"The command port"},
        "5027": {"comment":"$11 to the command port after an error"},
        "5031": {"comment":"Bit 3: $F4"},
        "5037": {"comment":"Bit 4: $F2"},
        "5043": {"comment":"Bit 5: $F3"},
        "5045": {"synopsis":"Returns the character in C with A = the result.","comment":"C = the character"},
        "5047": {"synopsis":"The RS232 card's function 2, the block function: writes (BLOCK_OUT_CHARS through RS232_PUT)\nor, on the input side, reads (RS232_BLOCK_IN) a block one character at a time.\nEntry: A = the code, DE = the block, BC = its length.","comment":"The input side?"},
        "5050": {"comment":"RS232_PUT for each byte"},
        "5053": {"comment":"BLOCK_OUT_CHARS"},
        "5056": {"synopsis":"Reads a block through RS232_GET, one character at a time (BLOCK_IN_CHARS).","comment":"RS232_GET for each byte"},
        "5059": {"comment":"BLOCK_IN_CHARS"},
        "5062": {"synopsis":"RS232_BAUD_TABLE: nine sound generator divider words for the RS232 line's speeds 0-8\n($0B69), read by RS_BAUD_CAPPED: the low byte goes to port 04h, bits 11-8 to port 05h bits\n3-0. The values rise from $0C88 (speed 0) to $0FFB (speed 8)."},
        "5080": {"synopsis":"RST $30 code $51/$D1, device 5 function 1, the cassette's character function: Reached from\nthe SYS low chip's CAS_CHAR through its CAS_TO_EXTH; calls CAS_CHAR_FN and returns its\nresult through CASX_BACK.\nObserved: SAVE writes the program's 16-byte header with it (C = each byte), LOAD and VERIFY\nread it back.","comment":"The character function"},
        "5085": {"synopsis":"RST $30 code $52/$D2, device 5 function 2, the cassette's block function (TAPE_BLOCK,\n$1630): writes or reads BC bytes at DE. Reached from the SYS low chip's CAS_BLOCK through\nits CAS_TO_EXTH; calls TAPE_BLOCK and returns its result through CASX_BACK.\nObserved: SAVE writes the program with it (DE = $19EF, BC = its length), which also ends the\noutput file; LOAD reads the program with it.","comment":"TAPE_BLOCK"},
        "5090": {"synopsis":"RST $30 code $53/$D3, device 5 function 3, opens a cassette file: Reached from the SYS low\nchip's CAS_F3 through its CAS_TO_EXTH; calls CAS_OPEN and returns its result through\nCASX_BACK.\nObserved: SAVE ($53), LOAD and VERIFY ($D3) and OPEN call it with DE = the name.","comment":"Open"},
        "5095": {"synopsis":"RST $30 code $54/$D4, device 5 function 4, closes a cassette file: Reached from the SYS low\nchip's CAS_F4 through its CAS_TO_EXTH; calls CAS_CLOSE and returns its result through\nCASX_BACK.\nObserved: SAVE, LOAD, VERIFY and CLOSE call it last.","comment":"Close"},
        "5100": {"synopsis":"RST $30 code $D5, device 5 function 5, compares BC bytes at DE with the tape (TAPE_VERIFY,\n$1605): Reached from the SYS low chip's CAS_F5 through its CAS_TO_EXTH; calls TAPE_VERIFY\nand returns its result through CASX_BACK. A data file is compared byte by byte (a difference\nfails with $E8); a program's block is read with $0BF1 = $FF, which makes the block reader\ncompare what it reads instead of storing it (TAPE_READ).\nObserved: VERIFY calls it with DE = $19EF, BC = the program's length.","comment":"TAPE_VERIFY"},
        "5105": {"synopsis":"The cassette's boot routine, reached from the SYS low chip's CAS_BOOT (the boot's\nBOOT_INIT_TABLE) through its CAS_TO_EXTH: TAPE_BOOT ($1707) clears the cassette's RAM\n$0BF0-$0E34, sets $0B6C to $80 and turns the tape motors off (port 05h bits 7-6). Falls into\nCASX_BACK.","comment":"TAPE_BOOT: clear the RAM, motors off"},
        "5108": {"synopsis":"Returns to the SYS low chip's CAS_NOP, and so to the caller, through $FFF0 (SYS in page 3).","comment":"The SYS low chip's CAS_NOP"},
        "5111": {"comment":"through $FFF0"},
        "5114": {"synopsis":"Opens a cassette file: the output side (code with bit 7 clear) at CAS_OPEN_OUT, the input\nside at CAS_OPEN_IN (falls into it).\nEntry: A = the code, DE = the name (a length byte, then the text).","comment":"The output side?"},
        "5117": {"synopsis":"Opens a cassette file for reading:\n1. An input file already open fails with $EB.\n2. Clears the input state $0BF3-$0D13 and keeps the name asked for at $0BF4 (CAS_COPY_NAME:\n   at most 16 characters, in capitals), then prints a new line, \"Searching\" and a new line.\n3. Reads header blocks into $0C05 (TAPE_READ, with $0D10 = the buffer, $0D09 = 256) until\n   one has the name asked for, or any name when none was given; prints \"Found: \" or\n   \"Reading: \" and the block's name for each.\n4. A failed read retries, except a break ($F5 in $0D0B), which closes the input and returns\n   $F5.\n5. With an output file open, a protected file (the header's third byte, $0D0C, not 0) closes\n   the input and fails with $E6.\n6. Keeps the file's type ($0BF3: $11 a program, $01 a data file) as $0B6B = type - $11,\n   takes the found name to $0BF4, points $0D07 past the name in the block and takes the name\n   off the count $0D05.\nExit: A = 0, DE = $0BF4, the name read; or an error.","comment":"An input file open already?"},
        "5120": {"comment":"$EB: already open"},
        "5123": {"comment":"The input state"},
        "5126": {"comment":"289 bytes: $0BF3-$0D13"},
        "5129": {"comment":"cleared"},
        "5132": {"comment":"The name asked for"},
        "5135": {"comment":"keep it in capitals"},
        "5138": {"comment":"A new line"},
        "5141": {"comment":"\"Searching\""},
        "5144": {"comment":"printed"},
        "5147": {"comment":"and a new line"},
        "5150": {"synopsis":"Reads the next header block from the tape into $0C05; a failed read tries again unless it\nwas a break.","comment":"$FF in $0D13 while searching"},
        "5155": {"comment":"The buffer"},
        "5158": {"comment":"into $0D10"},
        "5161": {"comment":"256 bytes at most"},
        "5167": {"comment":"No error yet"},
        "5177": {"comment":"Read a block (TAPE_READ)"},
        "5180": {"comment":"Got one?"},
        "5182": {"comment":"The read's error"},
        "5185": {"comment":"A break?"},
        "5187": {"comment":"No: read the next"},
        "5189": {"synopsis":"Gives the input file up: clears $0B6F and $0BF3 (no input file) and returns A, the error.","comment":"$0B6F = 0"},
        "5195": {"comment":"No input file"},
        "5200": {"comment":"A = the error"},
        "5201": {"synopsis":"A header block is in: compares its name at $0C05 with the one asked for; an empty name\nmatches any. HL' is the message: \"Found: \" or, on a match, \"Reading: \".","comment":"\"Found: \" unless it matches"},
        "5205": {"comment":"The block's name"},
        "5208": {"comment":"kept for the print"},
        "5209": {"comment":"The name asked for"},
        "5212": {"comment":"Its length"},
        "5213": {"comment":"None: any file"},
        "5216": {"comment":"Length and text"},
        "5217": {"comment":"compared"},
        "5218": {"synopsis":"Compares the next byte of the two names (the length byte first)."},
        "5219": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "5224": {"comment":"The whole name?"},
        "5226": {"synopsis":"The names match: the message becomes \"Reading: \".","comment":"\"Reading: \""},
        "5230": {"synopsis":"Prints the message and the block's name (when it has one) and a new line; a name that does\nnot match goes back to the search.","comment":"HL = the message"},
        "5231": {"comment":"Keep Z: a match"},
        "5232": {"comment":"printed"},
        "5235": {"comment":"The block's name"},
        "5237": {"comment":"Has it one?"},
        "5239": {"comment":"printed"},
        "5242": {"comment":"A new line"},
        "5245": {"comment":"Z: a match?"},
        "5247": {"comment":"No: the next file"},
        "5249": {"comment":"An output file open?"},
        "5255": {"comment":"Protected (the header's third byte)?"},
        "5259": {"comment":"0: fine"},
        "5262": {"comment":"Cleared"},
        "5264": {"comment":"$E6: protected"},
        "5266": {"comment":"Give the input up"},
        "5269": {"synopsis":"The file is open: keeps $0B6B = type - $11 (0 for a program), takes the block's name (at\nmost 16) to $0BF4 and sets the read pointer $0D07 and the count $0D05 past it.","comment":"The file's type"},
        "5272": {"comment":"0 for a program"},
        "5277": {"comment":"Searching over"},
        "5282": {"comment":"The block's name"},
        "5285": {"comment":"to $0BF4"},
        "5288": {"comment":"Its length"},
        "5289": {"comment":"16 at most?"},
        "5293": {"comment":"Cut to 16"},
        "5295": {"synopsis":"Copies the length byte and the name.","comment":"With the length byte"},
        "5301": {"comment":"The block's name"},
        "5304": {"comment":"Its length"},
        "5305": {"comment":"and the length byte"},
        "5308": {"comment":"Past the name"},
        "5309": {"comment":"The read pointer"},
        "5312": {"comment":"The bytes in the block"},
        "5316": {"comment":"less the name"},
        "5321": {"comment":"DE = the name"},
        "5324": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "5327": {"synopsis":"Opens a cassette file for writing:\n1. An output file already open fails with $EB; a protected input file open ($0D0C not 0)\n   fails with $E6.\n2. Clears the output state $0D14-$0E33 and keeps the name at $0D15 (CAS_COPY_NAME).\n3. The type $0D14 (also $0E2F, the bytes before the first block is written) is $11 when\n   $0B6B is 0 (a program: SAVE) and $01 otherwise (a data file: OPEN). $0E30 takes $0B6D\n   (then cleared), $0E32 = $FF.\n4. The buffer $0D26 ($0E2C) starts with the name; $0E26 counts its bytes and $0E28 points\n   past them.\nExit: A = 0, DE = $0D15.\nObserved: SAVE \"ab\" gives $0D14 = $11, OPEN OUTPUT $01, and a data file's first character\nwrites the header block.","comment":"An output file open already?"},
        "5330": {"comment":"$EB: already open"},
        "5333": {"comment":"A protected input file open?"},
        "5337": {"comment":"$E6: protected"},
        "5340": {"comment":"The output state"},
        "5343": {"comment":"288 bytes: $0D14-$0E33"},
        "5346": {"comment":"cleared"},
        "5349": {"comment":"The name"},
        "5352": {"comment":"kept in capitals"},
        "5355": {"comment":"0: a program"},
        "5359": {"comment":"$01: a data file"},
        "5363": {"comment":"$11: a program"},
        "5365": {"synopsis":"Sets the file's type and the output buffer, starting with the name.","comment":"The type"},
        "5368": {"comment":"and the bytes before the first block"},
        "5371": {"comment":"$0B6D"},
        "5375": {"comment":"used once"},
        "5377": {"comment":"into $0E30"},
        "5380": {"comment":"$FF"},
        "5385": {"comment":"The name"},
        "5388": {"comment":"The buffer"},
        "5391": {"comment":"its start in $0E2C"},
        "5395": {"comment":"The length"},
        "5396": {"comment":"and the length byte"},
        "5399": {"comment":"the count in $0E26"},
        "5403": {"comment":"The name into the buffer"},
        "5405": {"comment":"The next free byte"},
        "5409": {"comment":"DE = the name"},
        "5414": {"synopsis":"Copies a file name (a length byte, then the text) from DE to HL, at most 16 characters, in\ncapitals: a-z become A-Z, and codes $90-$98 become $80-$88 (the small accented letters to\ntheir capitals: RAM_CHARSET's glyphs $90-$98 and $80-$88).\nEntry: DE = the name, HL = the destination.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL.","comment":"HL = the name, DE = the destination"},
        "5415": {"comment":"Its length"},
        "5416": {"comment":"16 at most?"},
        "5420": {"comment":"Cut to 16"},
        "5422": {"synopsis":"Stores the length; an empty name ends here.","comment":"The length"},
        "5423": {"comment":"Empty?"},
        "5426": {"synopsis":"Takes the next character in capitals."},
        "5428": {"comment":"The character"},
        "5429": {"comment":"Below \"a\"?"},
        "5433": {"comment":"Above \"z\"?"},
        "5437": {"comment":"A capital"},
        "5441": {"synopsis":"Codes $90-$98 become $80-$88.","comment":"Below $90?"},
        "5445": {"comment":"Above $98?"},
        "5449": {"comment":"$80-$88"},
        "5451": {"synopsis":"Stores the character; the next one."},
        "5455": {"synopsis":"Clears BC bytes from HL.\nEntry: HL = the start, BC = the count (not 0).\nChanges: AF, BC, HL."},
        "5459": {"comment":"All done?"},
        "5464": {"synopsis":"Closes a cassette file. The input side (code with bit 7 set) at CAS_CLOSE_IN. The output\nside: an open file writes its buffer as the last block (TAPE_WRITE, with $0E2B = $FF),\nunless $0E2A says it was ended already, then clears the output state (CAS_OUT_CLOSED); an\nerror from the write is returned.\nEntry: A = the code.","comment":"The input side?"},
        "5467": {"comment":"An output file open?"},
        "5470": {"comment":"No: nothing to write"},
        "5478": {"synopsis":"Writes the buffer from $0E2C as the file's last block ($0E2B = $FF), unless $0E2A is set\n(ended already); then closes the output. CAS_BLOCK's output side (at $16DB) comes here after\nsetting $0E26/$0E2C to the program's block.\nExit: A = 0, or the write's error.","comment":"$FF: the last block"},
        "5483": {"comment":"Ended already?"},
        "5489": {"comment":"Write the block (TAPE_WRITE)"},
        "5492": {"comment":"Written?"},
        "5494": {"comment":"Keep the error"},
        "5495": {"comment":"Close anyway"},
        "5498": {"comment":"A = the error"},
        "5500": {"synopsis":"No output file: clears $0D14 and $0E2A and $0B6F; A = 0.","comment":"A = 0"},
        "5501": {"comment":"No output file"},
        "5504": {"comment":"Not ended"},
        "5509": {"synopsis":"Closes the input side: clears $0BF3 (no input file), $0D0C and $0B6F; A = 0.","comment":"A = 0"},
        "5510": {"comment":"No input file"},
        "5513": {"comment":"Not protected"},
        "5516": {"synopsis":"Clears the word at $0B6F and returns."},
        "5523": {"synopsis":"The cassette's character function: the output side (code with bit 7 clear) writes C to the\nfile ($1653), the input side reads one (CAS_GET, falls into it).\nEntry: A = the code; C = the character to write.","comment":"The output side?"},
        "5526": {"synopsis":"Reads a character from the input file. No input file fails with $E9; an error left in $0D0B\nfrom an earlier read is returned once (then $EC stays there); otherwise goes on at\nCAS_GET_BYTE.\nExit: A = 0 and C = the character, or an error.","comment":"An input file open?"},
        "5529": {"comment":"No: $E9"},
        "5530": {"comment":"An error left from before?"},
        "5533": {"comment":"Then return it"},
        "5534": {"synopsis":"Takes the next byte of the block in the buffer ($0D07, $0D05 left); with none left reads the\nnext block (CAS_NEXT_BLOCK). The block functions call it for each byte of a data file.","comment":"Bytes left in the block"},
        "5538": {"comment":"None?"},
        "5542": {"synopsis":"Takes the byte at the read pointer $0D07 into C and counts $0D05 down.","comment":"The read pointer"},
        "5545": {"comment":"C = the byte"},
        "5550": {"comment":"One fewer left"},
        "5557": {"synopsis":"With no bytes left, copies $0D0E (set when the file's last block has been read; observed:\n$0B6E is $FF after LOAD and VERIFY) to $0B6E, the end-of-file flag; A = 0.","comment":"The last byte taken?"},
        "5561": {"comment":"Then the end-of-file flag"},
        "5564": {"comment":"from $0D0E"},
        "5567": {"synopsis":"A = 0: success."},
        "5569": {"synopsis":"The block is used up: only a data file ($0BF3 = 1) goes on, a program fails with $E7. Reads\nthe next 256-byte block into $0C05 (CAS_READ_BLOCK) and takes its first byte.","comment":"A data file?"},
        "5573": {"comment":"$E7: not a data file"},
        "5576": {"comment":"256 bytes at most"},
        "5582": {"comment":"The buffer"},
        "5585": {"comment":"for the read"},
        "5588": {"comment":"and the read pointer"},
        "5591": {"synopsis":"Reads the next block (to $0D10, at most $0D09 bytes) unless the last one was read already\n($0D0E). Then a data file takes its first byte (CAS_GET_NEXT); a program returns A = 0 with\ncarry set. A failed read, or no block left, ends the input (CAS_IN_END). CAS_BLOCK's input\nside (at $164D) calls it for a program, with $0D10/$0D09 set to the destination.","comment":"The last block read already?"},
        "5595": {"comment":"$EC: nothing more"},
        "5597": {"comment":"No: read a block"},
        "5600": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "5602": {"comment":"A data file?"},
        "5606": {"comment":"Then take its first byte"},
        "5608": {"comment":"A program: A = 0"},
        "5609": {"comment":"carry: read"},
        "5611": {"synopsis":"Records the error A in $0D0B and returns it (CAS_IN_END). TAPE_VERIFY comes here with $E8\nwhen a byte differs.","comment":"Record the error"},
        "5614": {"synopsis":"Ends the input: returns the error in $0D0B and leaves $EC there for later reads, marks the\nlast block read ($0D0E = $FF), no bytes left and the end of the file ($0B6E = $FF).","comment":"The error"},
        "5617": {"comment":"returned"},
        "5618": {"comment":"$EC from now on"},
        "5620": {"synopsis":"Marks the end: $0D0E = $FF, no bytes left ($0D05 = 0) and the end-of-file flag $0B6E = $FF;\nreturns A as it is. CAS_BLOCK's input side ends here after a program's block.\nObserved: $0B6E is $FF after LOAD and VERIFY.","comment":"No more blocks"},
        "5625": {"comment":"No bytes left"},
        "5631": {"comment":"The end of the file"},
        "5637": {"synopsis":"RST $30 code $55 (device 5 function 5, through CASX_VERIFY): verifies what was saved against\nmemory. A file read in buffered mode ($0BF3 = 1) is read character by character through\n$159E and each character compared with the next byte at DE; any other file has its next\nblock read by TAPE_READ with $0BF1 set, so that the bytes are compared instead of stored.\nEither way the input file is closed after.\nEntry: DE = the bytes to compare with, BC = their count.\nExit: A = 0 when they match; $E9 when no input file is open, $E8 on a mismatch, an earlier\ninput error otherwise (TAPE_IN_ERROR).","comment":"No input file open?"},
        "5641": {"comment":"An input error still to report?"},
        "5645": {"comment":"Compare, do not store"},
        "5650": {"comment":"File type 1 (buffered)?"},
        "5654": {"comment":"No: verify the whole block at TRB_DISPATCH"},
        "5656": {"synopsis":"The buffered compare loop: one character from $159E against the byte at DE, BC times."},
        "5658": {"comment":"C = the next character of the file"},
        "5661": {"comment":"Keep it in L"},
        "5664": {"comment":"Read error?"},
        "5666": {"comment":"The same as in memory?"},
        "5670": {"comment":"No: error $E8, close the input"},
        "5673": {"comment":"Next byte in memory"},
        "5675": {"comment":"All BC compared?"},
        "5680": {"synopsis":"RST $30 code $52 / $D2 (device 5 function 2, through CASX_BLOCK): the block function. The\nsign flag set by the dispatch picks the direction: code $52 (positive) writes, at\nTAPE_WR_BLOCK; code $D2 reads, falling into TAPE_RD_BLOCK.","comment":"Writing?"},
        "5683": {"synopsis":"Reads BC bytes of the input file to DE. A buffered file (type 1) is read character by\ncharacter through $159E by BLOCK_IN_CHARS; any other file has its next block read from tape\nstraight into memory by $15D7 (TAPE_READ), and the input file is closed after.\nEntry: DE = where to, BC = how many.\nExit: A = 0 on success, an error code otherwise ($E9 no input file).","comment":"No input file open?"},
        "5687": {"comment":"An input error still to report?"},
        "5691": {"comment":"File type 1 (buffered)?"},
        "5695": {"synopsis":"Picks the way to read by the file type tested before (Z: buffered); also entered from\nTAPE_VERIFY.","comment":"Buffered: BLOCK_IN_CHARS reads BC characters through $159E"},
        "5701": {"comment":"The block goes straight to DE"},
        "5705": {"comment":"No more than BC bytes"},
        "5709": {"comment":"Read the block from tape"},
        "5712": {"comment":"Close the input file"},
        "5715": {"synopsis":"RST $30 code $51 (device 5 function 1, through CASX_CHAR's $1593): writes the character C to\nthe output file. Characters collect in the buffer at $0D26; a full buffer (256) is written\nto tape as a block by TAPE_FLUSH. The first block of a file is its header: it is written\nonce $0E2F characters have come (1 for a buffered file, so the header holds only the name;\n$11 for an unbuffered one, whose first 16 characters complete the header).\nEntry: C = the character.\nExit: A = 0 on success; $E9 no output file, $EC after an earlier write error, another code\nfrom TAPE_WRITE.","comment":"No output file open?"},
        "5719": {"synopsis":"TAPE_WR_CHAR without the open-file test: the routine TAPE_WR_BLOCK hands to BLOCK_OUT_CHARS\nto write a buffered file's block one character at a time.","comment":"An earlier write failed?"},
        "5726": {"comment":"Keep the character"},
        "5730": {"comment":"Characters still due before the header?"},
        "5735": {"comment":"None: just buffer it"},
        "5737": {"comment":"Count one; the last one writes the header"},
        "5741": {"synopsis":"Puts the character into the buffer, or writes the full buffer first (TAPE_FLUSH).","comment":"Bytes in the buffer"},
        "5745": {"comment":"All 256 used?"},
        "5751": {"comment":"Yes: write it, the character starts the next"},
        "5754": {"comment":"One more byte"},
        "5759": {"comment":"Store at the buffer pointer"},
        "5764": {"comment":"Advance it"},
        "5767": {"comment":"A = 0: done"},
        "5769": {"synopsis":"Writes the output buffer ($0D26, $0E26 bytes) to tape as one block (TAPE_WRITE), then starts\nthe buffer again with the character held in $0E2E.\nExit: carry set and A = 0 on success; carry clear and A = the error otherwise, with $0E2A\nmarked ($FF).","comment":"The block's bytes start at the buffer"},
        "5775": {"comment":"Write the block"},
        "5778": {"comment":"Written?"},
        "5780": {"synopsis":"A failed write: marks the output file as failed ($0E2A from 0 to $FF) and returns the error.","comment":"Mark the output file failed"},
        "5785": {"synopsis":"Starts the buffer again: one byte, the held character.","comment":"One byte in the buffer"},
        "5791": {"comment":"The character that did not fit"},
        "5797": {"comment":"First in the buffer"},
        "5799": {"comment":"The pointer after it"},
        "5802": {"comment":"A = 0, carry set: written"},
        "5805": {"synopsis":"Writes BC bytes from DE to the output file (device 5 function 2, code $52). A buffered file\n(type 1) is written character by character by BLOCK_OUT_CHARS through TAPE_PUT_CHAR. An\nunbuffered file writes any header still due (TAPE_FLUSH), then the bytes as the data block\n(the close path at $1566 with $0E26 = BC and $0E2C = DE), and the output file is closed\nafter.\nEntry: DE = the bytes, BC = their count.\nExit: A = 0 on success, an error code otherwise ($E9 no output file, $EC after an earlier\nerror).","comment":"No output file open?"},
        "5809": {"comment":"File type 1 (buffered)?"},
        "5813": {"comment":"Yes: BLOCK_OUT_CHARS writes BC characters through TAPE_PUT_CHAR"},
        "5819": {"comment":"An earlier write failed?"},
        "5828": {"comment":"Header still due? (and clear the count)"},
        "5834": {"comment":"Carry set: nothing to write"},
        "5836": {"comment":"Write the header block first"},
        "5841": {"comment":"Header failed?"},
        "5843": {"comment":"The data block: BC bytes"},
        "5847": {"comment":"from DE"},
        "5851": {"comment":"Write it and close the output file"},
        "5854": {"synopsis":"Turns a tape motor on or off (port 05h bits 7-6, kept in $0B12). A = 0 chooses the reading\nmotor (bit 6), any other A the writing one (bit 7); a set bit in $0B6C swaps that choice\n(bit 6 for reading, bit 7 for writing). $0B6C is $80 after boot, so both use bit 6.\nEntry: A = 0 reading, nonzero writing; D = 0 on, nonzero off.\nChanges: AF, L; enables interrupts.","comment":"Bit 6: the reading motor"},
        "5856": {"comment":"Reading?"},
        "5859": {"comment":"No: bit 7, the writing motor"},
        "5860": {"synopsis":"Swaps to the other motor bit when $0B6C asks for it.","comment":"Swapped for this direction?"},
        "5866": {"comment":"Yes: the other bit"},
        "5870": {"synopsis":"Sets the motor bit in the port 05h copy, or clears it again when D is not zero."},
        "5871": {"comment":"The port 05h copy, motor on"},
        "5875": {"comment":"Turning it off?"},
        "5879": {"comment":"Yes: clear the bit again"},
        "5880": {"synopsis":"Writes port 05h and its copy $0B12, enables interrupts.","comment":"The motors and the sound bits"},
        "5882": {"comment":"Remember them"},
        "5887": {"synopsis":"Turns both tape motors off: clears port 05h bits 7-6 and their copy in $0B12."},
        "5888": {"comment":"Both motor bits off"},
        "5895": {"synopsis":"Device 5's boot routine (through CASX_BOOT, from the SYS low chip's CAS_BOOT): clears the\ncassette's RAM $0BF0-$0E34 (input and output state and buffers), clears $0B6D, $0B6E and the\nCRC preset $0B6F, sets $0B6C to $80 (both directions on the bit 6 motor, TAPE_MOTOR) and\nturns both motors off.","comment":"Clear $0BF0-$0E34"},
        "5908": {"comment":"No protection for the next file"},
        "5914": {"comment":"The CRC starts from 0"},
        "5920": {"comment":"Both directions use the bit 6 motor"},
        "5925": {"comment":"Motors off"},
        "5936": {"synopsis":"Prints a length-prefixed string on the screen, a character at a time through RST $30 code\n$21 (the editor's write at the cursor).\nEntry: HL = the length byte.","comment":"B = the length"},
        "5937": {"synopsis":"Prints the next character of the string."},
        "5940": {"comment":"The character"},
        "5941": {"comment":"Write it at the cursor"},
        "5948": {"synopsis":"Prints a new line (MSG_NEWLINE) through TAPE_PRINT."},
        "5953": {"synopsis":"The length-prefixed new line printed by TAPE_NEWLINE: 2, then CR and LF."},
        "5956": {"synopsis":"\"Reading: \", length 9: printed by the open-input code at $146A before a file name that\nmatches the one asked for."},
        "5966": {"synopsis":"\"Searching\", length 9: printed by the open-input code at $1415 before the tape is read."},
        "5976": {"synopsis":"\"Found:   \", length 9: printed by the open-input code at $1451 before the name of a file\nfound on tape."},
        "5986": {"synopsis":"Tests for an open input file and ends any verify ($0BF1 = 0).\nExit: Z when none is open ($0BF3 = 0), with A = $E9; NZ otherwise.","comment":"Not verifying"},
        "5990": {"comment":"The input file's type, 0 when none"},
        "5995": {"synopsis":"Tests for an open output file.\nExit: Z when none is open ($0D14 = 0), with A = $E9; NZ otherwise.","comment":"The output file's type, 0 when none"},
        "5998": {"synopsis":"Sets Z from the type, A = $E9 for the caller to return."},
        "5999": {"comment":"$E9: no file open"},
        "6002": {"synopsis":"Reports an input error once: when $0D0B holds an error it returns it and leaves $EC in its\nplace, so later calls fail with $EC.\nExit: Z when there is none; NZ and A = the error otherwise."},
        "6005": {"comment":"The pending input error"},
        "6007": {"comment":"None?"},
        "6008": {"comment":"Later calls get $EC"},
        "6011": {"synopsis":"Reads one block from tape (unexercised by the coverage run; read from the code):\n1. Starts the reading motor, sets the hardware up (TAPE_HW_SETUP) and saves SP in $0E33 for\n   the error exits.\n2. Searches for the pilot: averages 32 cycles, then needs 1024 more cycles each within 2\n   counts of that average (else starts again); their average is the bit threshold D.\n3. Averages the two kinds of half-period (128 each), then waits for a half 4 or more counts\n   longer than expected: the sync; its second half follows.\n4. Reads the block (TAPE_RD_BYTE): a byte outside the CRC, $6A, the block type (must be\n   $0D13's; a data block while a header is wanted is skipped, back to 2), the file type into\n   $0BF3, the protection flag into $0D0C, the sector count; then per sector its number (must\n   be $0D0D's), its length (0 = 256), the bytes (stored at $0D10, or compared while $0BF1 is\n   set), the end marker into $0D0E and the CRC.\n5. Restores the hardware (TAPE_HW_RESTORE).\nEntry: $0D10 = where to, $0D09 = the room there, $0D13 = the block type wanted ($FF a\nheader).\nExit: carry set and A = 0 on success, with $0D05 = the bytes read; on an error A = its code\nwith carry clear, $0D0B set, returning to the caller from any depth (TAPE_ABORT).","comment":"For the error exits"},
        "6016": {"comment":"Reading motor on"},
        "6020": {"comment":"Tape hardware ready, interrupts off"},
        "6023": {"synopsis":"Starts the search for a steady pilot again, without the border stripes.","comment":"No border stripes while searching"},
        "6028": {"comment":"Clear the 24-bit sum HL':B'"},
        "6034": {"comment":"Sound divisor $DC: the delay before counting"},
        "6038": {"comment":"Wait for an edge of the input"},
        "6043": {"comment":"Sum 32 cycle counts"},
        "6049": {"synopsis":"Adds the count of one cycle to HL, 32 times.","comment":"E = the cycle's count"},
        "6055": {"comment":"H = sum / 32"},
        "6059": {"comment":"Round it"},
        "6062": {"comment":"D = the average cycle"},
        "6063": {"comment":"Then 1024 steady cycles"},
        "6066": {"synopsis":"Counts one more cycle, adds it to the 24-bit sum and checks it is within 2 of D."},
        "6069": {"comment":"Add the count to HL':B'"},
        "6075": {"synopsis":"Compares the count with the average D."},
        "6076": {"comment":"How far from the average?"},
        "6082": {"synopsis":"Is the difference 3 or more? Then the pilot is not steady: search again.","comment":"3 or more off?"},
        "6086": {"comment":"Next of the 1024"},
        "6091": {"comment":"Sum / 1024: H' = HL' / 4"},
        "6098": {"comment":"Round it"},
        "6104": {"comment":"Keep the threshold for the bits"},
        "6105": {"comment":"Border stripes from now on"},
        "6110": {"comment":"Divisor $E8 for the sync search"},
        "6114": {"comment":"Wait for an edge"},
        "6117": {"comment":"Two sums, for alternate halves"},
        "6121": {"comment":"256 halves"},
        "6123": {"synopsis":"Times one half-period and adds it twice to one of the two sums, which swap each time.","comment":"Swap to the other sum"},
        "6124": {"comment":"E = this half's count"},
        "6131": {"comment":"D = this kind's average half"},
        "6136": {"comment":"The other sum"},
        "6137": {"comment":"Rounded: H = the other kind's average"},
        "6142": {"comment":"L = this kind's"},
        "6143": {"comment":"D = the bit threshold again"},
        "6144": {"comment":"One half, to keep the alternation"},
        "6147": {"synopsis":"Times the next half and compares it with the average of its kind: the sync is a half 4 or\nmore counts longer.","comment":"Expect the other kind"},
        "6150": {"comment":"Time the half"},
        "6153": {"comment":"Longer than expected?"},
        "6156": {"comment":"Up to 2 shorter: still the pilot"},
        "6160": {"comment":"Much shorter: search again"},
        "6163": {"synopsis":"A half longer than expected: under 4 counts it is still the pilot.","comment":"4 or more longer?"},
        "6167": {"synopsis":"The sync's first half has come: times its second half, then reads the block.","comment":"Divisor $DC for the bits"},
        "6171": {"comment":"The sync's second half"},
        "6174": {"comment":"No bytes yet"},
        "6178": {"comment":"Where the bytes go"},
        "6182": {"comment":"The byte before the CRC'd part"},
        "6186": {"comment":"Start the CRC from the preset"},
        "6189": {"comment":"DE' = the room left"},
        "6194": {"comment":"The sync byte"},
        "6197": {"comment":"$6A?"},
        "6199": {"comment":"No: search again"},
        "6202": {"comment":"The block type"},
        "6205": {"comment":"The one wanted?"},
        "6211": {"comment":"Wanting a header?"},
        "6214": {"comment":"Yes: skip this block, search again"},
        "6217": {"comment":"No: error $EA"},
        "6220": {"synopsis":"The block type matches: reads the block's four header bytes, then the sectors.","comment":"Keep the block type"},
        "6223": {"comment":"The file type ($11 or $01)"},
        "6229": {"comment":"The protection flag"},
        "6235": {"comment":"The sector count"},
        "6239": {"comment":"Kept across the sectors"},
        "6242": {"synopsis":"The next sector: the CRC starts again from the preset."},
        "6243": {"comment":"The CRC from the preset"},
        "6248": {"synopsis":"Reads a sector's number (the expected one, or error $EA) and its length.","comment":"The sector number"},
        "6251": {"comment":"The one expected?"},
        "6255": {"comment":"No: error $EA"},
        "6258": {"comment":"The sector's length, 0 = 256"},
        "6262": {"synopsis":"Reads one byte of a sector and stores or compares it.","comment":"The byte"},
        "6265": {"comment":"Kept in A'"},
        "6266": {"comment":"Any room left? (count it down)"},
        "6271": {"comment":"No: error $E7 or $E8"},
        "6274": {"comment":"A buffered file is stored"},
        "6280": {"comment":"Verifying?"},
        "6286": {"comment":"The same as in memory?"},
        "6292": {"comment":"No: error $E8"},
        "6295": {"synopsis":"Stores the byte at IX."},
        "6299": {"synopsis":"Counts the byte and loops for the rest of the sector.","comment":"Next address"},
        "6301": {"comment":"One more byte read"},
        "6305": {"comment":"The end marker ($FF: the file's last sector)"},
        "6311": {"comment":"The CRC so far, onto the stack"},
        "6314": {"comment":"The CRC's low byte"},
        "6317": {"comment":"Carry clear for the compare"},
        "6319": {"comment":"BC = the CRC computed"},
        "6321": {"comment":"The CRC's high byte"},
        "6328": {"comment":"The one read the same?"},
        "6330": {"comment":"The sector count back"},
        "6331": {"comment":"No: error $EA"},
        "6333": {"comment":"The bytes read so far"},
        "6337": {"comment":"Where the next sector goes"},
        "6341": {"comment":"The next sector's number"},
        "6346": {"comment":"The room left"},
        "6351": {"comment":"Next sector"},
        "6353": {"comment":"A buffered file?"},
        "6359": {"comment":"A header block?"},
        "6366": {"comment":"A data block must fill the room exactly"},
        "6369": {"comment":"Room left: error $E7 or $E8"},
        "6371": {"synopsis":"The block is in: restores the hardware and returns A = 0 with carry set."},
        "6374": {"synopsis":"CTRL and ESC held while writing: marks the output file failed with $F5.","comment":"$F5: broken off"},
        "6381": {"synopsis":"CTRL and ESC held while reading: input error $F5."},
        "6386": {"synopsis":"Sets bit 3 of $0B62 for the break, waits a short while and leaves through TAPE_ABORT.","comment":"Bit 3 of $0B62: broken off"},
        "6393": {"synopsis":"A delay loop of 256 turns."},
        "6397": {"synopsis":"Error $EA: a wrong block type or sector number, or a bad CRC.","comment":"$EA: a bad block"},
        "6401": {"synopsis":"The bytes on tape do not fit the room: error $E7, or $E8 while verifying.","comment":"Verifying?"},
        "6405": {"comment":"$E7 when not"},
        "6409": {"synopsis":"Error $E8: verifying found a difference."},
        "6411": {"synopsis":"Records the error in $0D0B, the input error, and falls into TAPE_ABORT.","comment":"The input error"},
        "6414": {"synopsis":"Leaves a tape transfer: restores the hardware (TAPE_HW_RESTORE), then returns the error in A\nwith carry clear to the caller of TAPE_READ or TAPE_WRITE, through the SP saved in $0E33."},
        "6415": {"comment":"Motors off, interrupts back"},
        "6419": {"comment":"Carry clear: failed"},
        "6420": {"comment":"Back to the transfer's caller"},
        "6425": {"synopsis":"Reads a byte from tape, least significant bit first: a cycle shorter than the threshold D is\na 1, a longer one a 0. Each bit goes into the CRC in HL' (TAPE_CRC_BIT).\nEntry: D = the threshold; C = the input level that ends a cycle.\nExit: A = the byte.\nChanges: AF, E, H.","comment":"The marker bit: 8 bits when it falls out"},
        "6427": {"synopsis":"Times one cycle and shifts its bit in from the top.","comment":"E = the cycle's count"},
        "6430": {"comment":"Shorter than the threshold?"},
        "6432": {"comment":"A = $FF for a 1, Z for a 0"},
        "6433": {"comment":"Into the CRC"},
        "6437": {"comment":"The bit in; the marker out after 8?"},
        "6443": {"synopsis":"Times the half-period now running: waits for the sound timer interrupt (started at the last\nedge), then counts polls of port 59h bit 5 until the input changes.\nExit: A = E = the count; C = the input level that has just ended.","comment":"Port 59h bit 5: the tape input"},
        "6447": {"comment":"C = the level the half will change to"},
        "6450": {"comment":"Count from 0"},
        "6452": {"comment":"The fixed delay of the timer"},
        "6456": {"synopsis":"Times a full cycle: waits for the sound timer interrupt, then counts polls of the input\nthrough one level and the other (TCI_FIRST, TCI_SECOND), ending where the input becomes C's\nlevel again. Restarts the timer at that edge.\nEntry: C = the level a cycle ends on ($20 or 0, as port 59h bit 5).\nExit: A = E = the count.","comment":"Count from 0"},
        "6458": {"comment":"The fixed delay of the timer"},
        "6460": {"synopsis":"Counts while the input stays at C's level (a count wrapping to 0 tests the break keys).","comment":"Count; every 256 test CTRL+ESC"},
        "6464": {"comment":"Still at C's level?"},
        "6471": {"synopsis":"Counts while the input is away from C's level; its change ends the count.","comment":"Count; every 256 test CTRL+ESC"},
        "6475": {"comment":"Still away from C's level?"},
        "6482": {"comment":"Restart the sound timer at this edge"},
        "6484": {"comment":"Clear the interrupt"},
        "6486": {"synopsis":"Border stripes: when $0BF0 is not zero, swaps the border (port 00h) between $88 and $A0 at\neach call. Falls into TAPE_ESC_TEST.","comment":"Stripes off?"},
        "6492": {"comment":"Swap $88 and $A0"},
        "6500": {"synopsis":"Writes the new border colour and its copy."},
        "6503": {"comment":"The border colour"},
        "6505": {"synopsis":"Tests CTRL and ESC (keyboard row 7, selected by TAPE_HW_SETUP, bits 4 and 3): both held\nbreaks the transfer off (TAPE_RD_BREAK).\nExit: A = E.","comment":"Keyboard row 7: CTRL and ESC"},
        "6507": {"comment":"Both held?"},
        "6512": {"comment":"Return the count"},
        "6514": {"synopsis":"Writes one block to tape (exercised by SAVE):\n1. Starts the writing motor, waits about a second (65536 turns of a delay loop) and sets the\n   hardware up (TAPE_HW_SETUP), border stripes on.\n2. The pilot: $14 x 256 cycles, twice as many ($28) for the file's first block ($0E32 not\n   zero); then one sync cycle and a byte $00.\n3. $6A, the block type ($0E32: $FF the header, 0 data), the file type ($0D14), the\n   protection flag ($0E30) and the sector count (the bytes in $0E26 rounded up to 256s), the\n   CRC in HL' starting from $0B6F.\n4. Each sector: its number ($0E31), its length (0 = 256), the bytes from $0E2C, an end\n   marker ($0E2B after the last sector, else 0) and the CRC's two bytes; the CRC starts\n   again from $0B6F for the next sector.\n5. Five more pilot cycles, then the hardware is restored (TAPE_HW_RESTORE).\nEntry: $0E2C = the bytes, $0E26 = their count.\nExit: carry set and A = 0 on success; carry clear and A = $F5 when broken off with CTRL+ESC.","comment":"For the error exits"},
        "6518": {"comment":"D = 0: on"},
        "6520": {"comment":"A = $FF: the writing motor"},
        "6524": {"comment":"A delay of 65536 turns"},
        "6527": {"synopsis":"The delay loop before the pilot (two EX (SP),HL a turn leave HL as it was)."},
        "6533": {"comment":"Tape hardware ready"},
        "6536": {"comment":"Border stripes on"},
        "6541": {"comment":"$14 x 256 pilot cycles"},
        "6544": {"comment":"The file's first block?"},
        "6550": {"comment":"Twice as long"},
        "6553": {"synopsis":"Writes the pilot, the sync and the block's first bytes.","comment":"The pilot"},
        "6556": {"comment":"The sync cycle"},
        "6562": {"comment":"$00, outside the CRC"},
        "6565": {"comment":"HL' = the CRC, from the preset"},
        "6569": {"comment":"The sync byte $6A"},
        "6574": {"comment":"The bytes start here"},
        "6578": {"comment":"The block type: $FF header, 0 data"},
        "6585": {"comment":"The file type"},
        "6592": {"comment":"The protection flag"},
        "6599": {"comment":"The byte count"},
        "6602": {"comment":"Whole 256s"},
        "6603": {"comment":"Plus a part?"},
        "6607": {"comment":"Counts as one more"},
        "6608": {"synopsis":"Writes the sector count."},
        "6613": {"synopsis":"The next sector: the CRC starts again from the preset."},
        "6614": {"comment":"The CRC from the preset"},
        "6618": {"synopsis":"Writes a sector's number and length, then its bytes.","comment":"The sector number"},
        "6625": {"comment":"Under 256 left?"},
        "6627": {"comment":"D = the bytes in this sector"},
        "6630": {"comment":"No: 256, written as 0"},
        "6632": {"synopsis":"Writes the sector's length."},
        "6636": {"synopsis":"Writes the sector's next byte.","comment":"The next byte"},
        "6641": {"comment":"One less to go"},
        "6645": {"comment":"The sector's end?"},
        "6648": {"comment":"The block's last sector?"},
        "6650": {"comment":"Its end marker"},
        "6655": {"comment":"Not the last: 0"},
        "6656": {"synopsis":"Writes the sector's end marker and its CRC, then moves on."},
        "6660": {"comment":"Keep the count"},
        "6662": {"comment":"The CRC, low byte first"},
        "6672": {"comment":"The bytes still to write"},
        "6675": {"comment":"and where they are"},
        "6679": {"comment":"The next sector's number"},
        "6686": {"comment":"More to write?"},
        "6690": {"comment":"Five pilot cycles to end"},
        "6696": {"comment":"Let the last half end"},
        "6698": {"comment":"The next block is not the first"},
        "6702": {"comment":"Restore and return A = 0, carry set"},
        "6705": {"synopsis":"Writes B x C pilot cycles (B = 0 counts 256), two pilot halves each.\nEntry: B, C = the counts.\nExit: B = C = 0.","comment":"Two halves: a cycle"},
        "6713": {"comment":"C times 256"},
        "6717": {"synopsis":"Writes the byte C, least significant bit first, a cycle per bit (shorter for a 1), each bit\ngoing into the CRC in HL' (TAPE_CRC_BIT).\nEntry: C = the byte.\nExit: C as it was.","comment":"8 bits"},
        "6719": {"synopsis":"Writes one bit: a half, the CRC, the other half.","comment":"The next bit into bit 7"},
        "6721": {"comment":"First half"},
        "6724": {"comment":"Z for a 0, NZ for a 1"},
        "6726": {"comment":"Into the CRC"},
        "6729": {"comment":"Second half"},
        "6735": {"synopsis":"Writes half a cycle for the bit in bit 7 of C: TAPE_DIVISORS' 1 or 0 divisor.","comment":"A 1 or a 0?"},
        "6739": {"comment":"The 1 divisor"},
        "6744": {"synopsis":"The 0 divisor."},
        "6749": {"synopsis":"Writes half a pilot cycle.","comment":"The pilot divisor"},
        "6754": {"synopsis":"Writes half a sync cycle.","comment":"The sync divisor"},
        "6757": {"synopsis":"Writes one half-period: waits for the sound timer interrupt that ends the previous half,\ntoggles the tape output (any access to ports 50h-57h), loads the divisor for the new half\ninto port 04h and restarts the timer (IN 5Bh), clearing the interrupt (OUT 07h). Then the\nborder stripes and the break test (TAPE_BORDER).\nEntry: A = the divisor.","comment":"Keep the divisor"},
        "6758": {"comment":"CTRL and ESC both held?"},
        "6765": {"comment":"Wait for the half to end"},
        "6767": {"comment":"Toggle the tape output"},
        "6770": {"comment":"The new half's divisor"},
        "6772": {"comment":"Restart the timer"},
        "6774": {"comment":"Clear the interrupt"},
        "6776": {"comment":"Stripes and break test"},
        "6780": {"synopsis":"Prepares the hardware for a transfer, interrupts off: writes 0 to ports 58h-5Bh and 04h, $FF\nto $0B71, selects keyboard row 7 (port 03h, keeping the card bits) for the break test, turns\nthe sound interrupt on in port 05h (bit 5, divisor high bits $F), clears $0B14, turns the\nCRTC cursor off (R10 = $23) so the frame interrupt stops, restarts the sound timer and puts\na RET at RAM $0038 (the old byte in $0BF2), so the timer's interrupt only ends a HALT."},
        "6781": {"comment":"Ports 58h-5Bh and 04h = 0"},
        "6792": {"comment":"$0B71 = $FF"},
        "6796": {"comment":"Keyboard row 7, card bits kept"},
        "6805": {"comment":"Bit 4 of the port 05h copy off"},
        "6813": {"comment":"Motor bits, sound interrupt on"},
        "6819": {"comment":"$0B14 = 0"},
        "6823": {"comment":"CRTC R10 = $23: no cursor, no frame interrupt"},
        "6831": {"comment":"Restart the sound timer"},
        "6833": {"comment":"Clear the interrupt"},
        "6835": {"comment":"RAM $0038 becomes RET"},
        "6841": {"comment":"Keep its old byte"},
        "6845": {"synopsis":"Ends a transfer: motors off (TAPE_MOTORS_OFF), ports 03h and 05h back from $0B11 and $0B12,\nthe CRTC cursor (and with it the frame interrupt) back on when bit 0 of $0B1F is set (R10 =\n$03), ports 5Bh, 5Ah, 59h and 58h from the bits of $0B1F, RAM $0038 back from $0BF2,\ninterrupts on.\nExit: A = 0, carry set."},
        "6846": {"comment":"Motors off"},
        "6849": {"comment":"Port 03h back"},
        "6854": {"comment":"Port 05h back"},
        "6859": {"comment":"Was the cursor interrupt on?"},
        "6867": {"comment":"CRTC R10 = $03: the cursor back"},
        "6875": {"synopsis":"Ports 5Bh-58h from successive bits of $0B1F.","comment":"Bit 6 for port 5Bh"},
        "6889": {"comment":"RAM $0038 back"},
        "6895": {"comment":"A = 0, carry set"},
        "6899": {"synopsis":"The sound divisors of the tape's half-periods (port 04h values; 256 minus each is the\ncount): $D6 the pilot (42), $DE a 1 bit (34), $CE a 0 bit (50), $BC the sync (68). Read by\nTAPE_PILOT_HALF, TAPE_BIT_HALF, TBH_ZERO and TAPE_SYNC_HALF."},
        "6903": {"synopsis":"Adds one bit to the tape CRC in HL': when the bit differs from bit 15, flips bits 11 and 4\nand shifts a 1 in, else shifts a 0 in.\nEntry: Z for a 0 bit, NZ for a 1; HL' = the CRC.\nExit: HL' updated.\nChanges: AF."},
        "6904": {"comment":"$80 for a 1"},
        "6908": {"comment":"0 for a 0"},
        "6909": {"synopsis":"Is the bit different from the CRC's top bit?","comment":"The bit against bit 15"},
        "6911": {"comment":"The same: shift a 0 in"},
        "6913": {"comment":"Flip bit 11"},
        "6917": {"comment":"Flip bit 4"},
        "6921": {"comment":"Shift a 1 in"},
        "6922": {"synopsis":"Shifts the CRC left with the carry."},
        "6926": {"synopsis":"The system call's two channel tables, copied by the boot ($1024) to RAM $0B00-$0B0F (see the\nSYS low chip's SYSCALL_DISPATCH): $0B00 (codes with bit 7 set) = FF 01 02 FF FF 05 06 FF,\n$0B08 (bit 7 clear) = 00 FF 02 FF 04 05 06 FF. Each byte is the device of an entry, $FF\nnone."},
        "6942": {"synopsis":"Code that runs in RAM: copied by the boot ($102E) to $0030-$003F. At $0030 (RST $30, the\nsystem call) it jumps to $0B23, the copy of RAM_SYSCALL; RAM_INT38 follows at $0038.","comment":"RAM $0030: the system call"},
        "6950": {"synopsis":"Code that runs in RAM at $0038 (the IM 1 interrupt): saves AF, puts SYS in page 3 (port 02h\n= $70) and jumps to the SYS low chip's INT_ENTRY ($C412), which leaves through\nRAM_INT_RETURN ($0B41).","comment":"RAM $0038: the interrupt"},
        "6951": {"comment":"SYS in page 3"},
        "6955": {"comment":"The SYS low chip's INT_ENTRY"},
        "6958": {"synopsis":"Code that runs in RAM at $0B23 (copied by the boot, $1035): the system call's entry. Takes\nthe code byte after the RST $30 (stepping the return address past it) into A', saves the\ncaller's AF' and the paging ($0003), puts SYS in page 3 and jumps to the SYS low chip's\nSYSCALL_ENTRY ($C363), which comes back through RAM_SC_RETURN ($0B37).","comment":"RAM $0B23: the return address"},
        "6959": {"comment":"The code byte after the RST"},
        "6961": {"comment":"Return past it"},
        "6962": {"comment":"The code into A'"},
        "6963": {"comment":"Save the caller's AF'"},
        "6964": {"comment":"Save the paging"},
        "6968": {"comment":"SYS in page 3"},
        "6975": {"comment":"The SYS low chip's SYSCALL_ENTRY"},
        "6978": {"synopsis":"Code that runs in RAM at $0B37: the system call's return. Keeps the result AF, restores the\npaging saved by RAM_SYSCALL (to $0003 and port 02h) and the caller's AF', and returns.","comment":"RAM $0B37: keep the result"},
        "6979": {"comment":"The saved paging"},
        "6983": {"comment":"Paging back"},
        "6985": {"comment":"The caller's AF'"},
        "6986": {"comment":"The result back in AF"},
        "6988": {"synopsis":"Code that runs in RAM at $0B41: the interrupt's return. Writes the paging in A back to $0003\nand port 02h, pops the AF RAM_INT38 saved, enables interrupts and returns.","comment":"RAM $0B41: the paging back"},
        "6993": {"comment":"The AF the interrupt saved"},
        "6996": {"synopsis":"\"MOPS\": compared by the boot's card scan ($107C) with the first 4 bytes of a card's ROM\n($C000) in a slot whose type (port 5Ah) is 3; a card that has it supplies its own\nlength-prefixed name at $C004 for the slot record, any other slot record is marked $FF."},
        "7000": {"synopsis":"Length 3, \"VGB\": the name the boot's card scan ($106E) copies into the slot record of a slot\nof type 1."},
        "7004": {"synopsis":"Length 5, \"RS232\": the name the boot's card scan ($1068) copies into the slot record of a\nslot of type 0. $1191 compares a slot's name with the text at $1B5D: a match runs EXTH's own\nRS232_FUNCS instead of the card's $C00D."},
        "7010": {"synopsis":"Length 4, \"DISK\": the name the boot's card scan ($1074) copies into the slot record of a\nslot of type 2."},
        "7015": {"synopsis":"\"CISL\": 4 letters with no reader found in this chip (no address of them is loaded and the\ncoverage run never read them)."},
        "7019": {"synopsis":"The RAM character set's glyphs, 10 bytes (scanlines) each, bit 7 the left dot. The boot\n($100E) copies the first 320 bytes to RAM $0740 for codes $80-$9F (the SYS chips draw code n\nfrom $0740 + (n - $80) x 10), then the last 10 bytes 64 times for codes $A0-$DF. By their\ndots:\n- $80-$88: capital accented letters: A, E, I, O with an acute, O with two dots, O with a\n  double acute, U with an acute, U with two dots, U with a double acute.\n- $89-$8E: box lines: down-right corner, up-right corner, vertical, vertical with right\n  branch, horizontal with down branch, cross.\n- $8F: an inverse A (drawn by the SYS low chip's ED_BLINK as a lock-state cursor).\n- $90-$98: the small letters a, e, i, o with an acute, o with two dots, o with a double\n  acute, u with an acute, u with two dots, u with a double acute.\n- $99-$9D: box lines: down-left corner, up-left corner, horizontal, vertical with left\n  branch, horizontal with up branch.\n- $9E, $9F: an inverse C and an inverse S (ED_BLINK's other lock-state cursors).\n- the 10 bytes at $1CAB: blank, the glyph of codes $A0-$DF."},
        "7349": {"synopsis":"PRINT USING for a number: prints the top number of the IY stack by the format field that\nstarts at the format pointer ($172E), leaves the pointer after the field and goes back to\nthe SYS high chip's $E67A (drop the number, mark the item printed). The SYS high chip's\nPRINT_EXPR enters here through EXTH_JUMP with USING active.\n1. Reads the field (USING_SCAN): '#' a digit place, '.' the point, ',' a thousands\n   separator, '*' / '%' at the start fill the unused places with '*' / '0', '$' a dollar\n   sign, '+' / '-' a sign place ('+' prints + or -, '-' prints - or a space), '<' / '>'\n   count as a digit place, four or more '^' the exponent (E+nn). The field ends at any other\n   character, at a second sign, '$' or '<'/'>' after a digit place; a second '.' or one to\n   three '^' is error 4.\n2. Fits the number (UN_FIELD_DONE): its integer digits must fit the places before the point,\n   less one for '$' and one for a sign (always for a negative number, or when '+'/'-' was\n   given), else error 4 (observed: \"##\" with 999).\n3. Prints the unused places (spaces, or the fill), the '$' and the sign before the fill or\n   right before the digits, a 0 for a number below 1 when a place is left, the integer\n   digits with the separators, the point and the fraction digits, truncated, not rounded\n   (\"##.##\" with 9.999 gave \" 9.99\"). '*' / '%' after the point print a space in place of a\n   trailing zero (\"#.***\" with 1.5 gave \"1.5  \").\n4. With '^' the integer places are all used, the exponent adjusted to suit, and printed as\n   E, a sign and two digits, a 0 before them for each '^' past four (\"#.##^^^^\" with 12345\n   gave \"1.23E+04\").\nObserved: \"##.##\" 3.14159 \" 3.14\", \"+####\" 42 \"  +42\", \"$###.##\" -5.5 \" $-5.50\", \"**###.##\"\n5.5 \"****5.50\", \"%%###\" -5 \"-0005\", \"##,###.##\" 12345.678 \"12,345.67\".\nEntry: IY = the number; ($172E) = the field's first character.\nExit: through the SYS high chip's $E67A; BC', DE', HL' are kept.","comment":"Keep the interpreter's BC', DE', HL'"},
        "7353": {"comment":"HL' = the format pointer: the field's start"},
        "7356": {"comment":"IY = the format pointer, the IY stack kept on the stack"},
        "7359": {"comment":"BC' = 0: no point found yet"},
        "7363": {"comment":"Clear the counts: L places, H after the point, D '^'s"},
        "7367": {"comment":"C = the flags, E = the fill character"},
        "7369": {"synopsis":"Reads the field's next character and runs its handler from USING_JUMPS; any other character\nends the field (UN_END_POP). A handler is entered with Z set when no digit place was counted\nyet (L = 0).","comment":"The next format character"},
        "7374": {"comment":"Keep the counts over the search"},
        "7376": {"comment":"One of the field characters?"},
        "7384": {"comment":"No: the field ends"},
        "7386": {"comment":"C = its index from the list's end, doubled"},
        "7388": {"comment":"Its handler from USING_JUMPS"},
        "7396": {"comment":"The flags back"},
        "7397": {"comment":"Handler on the stack, the counts back in HL"},
        "7398": {"comment":"Z: no digit place yet"},
        "7400": {"comment":"To the handler"},
        "7401": {"synopsis":"The '+' handler: A = $40 (bit 6 of C, the '+' sign). The JP C (never taken: carry is clear)\nhides LD A,$80 at $1CEC, the '-' handler's entry from USING_JUMPS.","comment":"'+': flag bit 6"},
        "7403": {"comment":"Never taken: hides LD A,$80, the '-' entry at $1CEC"},
        "7406": {"synopsis":"A sign character: after a digit place it ends the field; else sets its flag (bit 6 '+', bit\n7 '-') in C, clearing the other sign's flag and bits 2-5.","comment":"After a digit place: the field ends"},
        "7409": {"comment":"Set the sign's flag"},
        "7412": {"comment":"Keep bits 0-1 and this sign's bit only"},
        "7416": {"comment":"Next character"},
        "7418": {"synopsis":"The '$' handler: after a digit place it ends the field, else sets bit 1 of C (print '$').","comment":"After a digit place: the field ends"},
        "7420": {"comment":"Bit 1: print a '$'"},
        "7424": {"synopsis":"The '<' and '>' handler: before any digit place one more place, after one the end of the\nfield (observed: \"<##>\" with 5 gave \"  5\").","comment":"After a digit place: the field ends"},
        "7426": {"comment":"One more digit place"},
        "7429": {"synopsis":"The '*' and '%' handler: a digit place. After the point one more place after it; before the\npoint the fill character for the unused places, '*' for '*' and '0' for '%' (observed:\n\"%%###\" with -5 gave \"-0005\").","comment":"One more place, counted after the point"},
        "7431": {"comment":"After the point (BC' set)?"},
        "7435": {"comment":"Yes: next character"},
        "7437": {"comment":"Before the point: not after it"},
        "7438": {"comment":"The character itself"},
        "7441": {"comment":"'*'?"},
        "7443": {"comment":"Fill with '*'"},
        "7446": {"comment":"'%': fill with '0'"},
        "7450": {"synopsis":"A field that cannot be used or a number that does not fit: error 4 (\"Bad argument\") through\nthe SYS high chip's ERROR_ENTRY.","comment":"Error 4, \"Bad argument\""},
        "7452": {"comment":"Through the SYS high chip's ERROR_ENTRY"},
        "7458": {"synopsis":"The '#' handler: one more digit place, counted after the point too once the point was seen.","comment":"One more digit place"},
        "7459": {"comment":"Before the point?"},
        "7463": {"comment":"Yes: next character"},
        "7465": {"comment":"After the point: one more there"},
        "7468": {"synopsis":"The '^' handler: counts it in D; the first '^' stands for the point when the field has none.","comment":"A point found already?"},
        "7471": {"comment":"Yes: just count"},
        "7473": {"comment":"No: BC' = this '^', the point's place"},
        "7477": {"synopsis":"Counts one more '^' in D."},
        "7478": {"comment":"One more '^'"},
        "7481": {"synopsis":"The '.' handler: keeps its address in BC'; a second point is error 4 (observed: \"##.##.##\").","comment":"A point already?"},
        "7484": {"comment":"Yes: error 4"},
        "7486": {"comment":"BC' = the point's address"},
        "7493": {"synopsis":"A character that is not a field character ends the field: drops the counts kept for the\nsearch.","comment":"The flags and counts back"},
        "7495": {"synopsis":"The field's end: with no point the place after the field stands for it (BC' = the character\nthat ended the field).","comment":"A point found?"},
        "7500": {"comment":"No: BC' = the character after the field"},
        "7504": {"synopsis":"The field is read: gives the IY stack back, keeps the places ($171C, L the digit places,\n$171D the places after the point) and checks the '^' count: four or more an exponent field,\none to three error 4, none a fixed field. A fixed field's L becomes the digits to print, its\ninteger digits plus its places after the point.","comment":"IY = the number again"},
        "7507": {"comment":"$171C = the digit places, $171D those after the point"},
        "7510": {"comment":"Four '^' or more?"},
        "7513": {"comment":"Yes: an exponent field"},
        "7515": {"comment":"One to three '^': error 4"},
        "7519": {"comment":"The exponent without its sign"},
        "7524": {"comment":"Its integer digits ($40: 1)"},
        "7526": {"comment":"Plus the places after the point"},
        "7528": {"synopsis":"A negative number (non-zero, its sign bit set) is made positive and bit 0 of C set (print\n'-'). The LD A,$C1 at $1D7F hides the POP BC at $1D80, where a positive number enters: both\npaths take the flags back.","comment":"Keep the flags"},
        "7529": {"comment":"The number 0?"},
        "7535": {"comment":"Its sign: negative?"},
        "7542": {"comment":"Clear the sign bit: its magnitude"},
        "7548": {"comment":"The flags back"},
        "7549": {"comment":"Bit 0: negative, print '-'"},
        "7551": {"comment":"Skips $1D80: a positive number's POP BC"},
        "7553": {"comment":"B = the integer digits (<= 0 below 1)"},
        "7559": {"comment":"DE' = the point's place"},
        "7563": {"comment":"H = 0: spare places, L = 0 digits to place"},
        "7566": {"comment":"An exponent field?"},
        "7569": {"comment":"Below 1: no integer digits to place"},
        "7573": {"comment":"L = the integer digits to place"},
        "7574": {"synopsis":"Walks the field back from the point to its start: each place left over by the integer digits\n(L) counts in H, the spare places; a ',' among the digits takes no place, one past them\ndoes."},
        "7575": {"comment":"The character before"},
        "7576": {"comment":"At the field's start?"},
        "7582": {"comment":"The start: count it too"},
        "7584": {"comment":"Before the start: done"},
        "7586": {"synopsis":"One character: no carry for a ',', carry for any other place.","comment":"A separator?"},
        "7590": {"comment":"Carry: a place"},
        "7591": {"synopsis":"An exponent field counts every place but ','; a fixed one gives a place to the next integer\ndigit while any are left.","comment":"An exponent field?"},
        "7595": {"comment":"Integer digits left to place?"},
        "7597": {"comment":"None: a spare place"},
        "7602": {"comment":"A ',' between digits takes no place"},
        "7604": {"comment":"One more digit placed"},
        "7605": {"comment":"Clear carry: no spare place"},
        "7606": {"synopsis":"An exponent field: a ',' is skipped, any other character is a place.","comment":"A ',': skip it"},
        "7608": {"synopsis":"Counts a spare place.","comment":"One more spare place"},
        "7611": {"synopsis":"Takes a place for the '$' and one for the sign (a negative number, or a '+'/'-' flag); no\nplace left (H negative) or integer digits left unplaced is error 4.","comment":"A '$' to print?"},
        "7615": {"comment":"It takes a place"},
        "7616": {"synopsis":"A negative number takes a sign place, as does a positive one with '+' or '-' given.","comment":"Negative?"},
        "7620": {"comment":"A '+' or '-' flag (bits 2-7)?"},
        "7625": {"synopsis":"The sign takes a place.","comment":"The sign's place"},
        "7626": {"synopsis":"No room for the sign and '$', or integer digits left over, is error 4.","comment":"Too few places?"},
        "7631": {"comment":"Integer digits that found no place?"},
        "7636": {"comment":"An exponent field?"},
        "7640": {"comment":"L = the integer digits (0 below 1)"},
        "7646": {"synopsis":"L = the integer digits to print (0 below 1); a number below 1 with a spare place left gets a\n0 before the point.","comment":"L = the integer digits"},
        "7647": {"comment":"Below 1 with a spare place?"},
        "7654": {"comment":"Bit 2: print a 0 before the point"},
        "7656": {"comment":"One digit, the 0"},
        "7660": {"synopsis":"An exponent field: every place before the point gets a digit, and the exponent B is lowered\nby their number.","comment":"L = the places before the point"},
        "7661": {"comment":"The exponent less those places"},
        "7664": {"synopsis":"With an exponent field or a fill character the sign (and '$') is printed now, before the\nfill (observed: \"**##\" with -5 gave \"-**5\"); otherwise the fill is a space and the sign\nwaits.","comment":"An exponent field?"},
        "7668": {"comment":"A fill character given?"},
        "7672": {"comment":"No: fill with spaces (Z stays: no sign yet)"},
        "7674": {"synopsis":"Prints the '$' and the sign before the fill (USING_SIGNS).","comment":"'$' and sign first"},
        "7677": {"comment":"Spare places to fill?"},
        "7678": {"synopsis":"Prints a fill character for each spare place (H), the last one replaced by a 0 when the\nnumber is below 1 (bit 2); an exponent field has no spare places.","comment":"One place less: all done?"},
        "7681": {"comment":"An exponent field?"},
        "7685": {"comment":"A 0 before the point wanted?"},
        "7689": {"comment":"The last spare place?"},
        "7691": {"comment":"Yes: sign, then fill '0'"},
        "7694": {"synopsis":"Prints the fill character and counts the place.","comment":"The fill character"},
        "7700": {"synopsis":"After space fill the '$' and sign are printed next to the digits; then DE' is set back from\nthe point by the integer digits to print (L), passing over ','s, to where the first digit\ngoes.","comment":"Space fill: the sign not printed yet?"},
        "7703": {"comment":"Yes: '$' and sign now"},
        "7706": {"comment":"DE' = the point's place"},
        "7710": {"comment":"Integer digits (B)?"},
        "7714": {"comment":"Positive: go back L places"},
        "7717": {"synopsis":"A number below 1: only the 0 (L = 1) was printed, so DE' stays at the point.","comment":"Just the 0?"},
        "7721": {"synopsis":"Moves DE' back one digit place for each integer digit left (L).","comment":"Digits left?"},
        "7722": {"synopsis":"One more integer digit placed: any left (L)?","comment":"One less: all placed?"},
        "7726": {"synopsis":"One character back, again while it is a ','.","comment":"One character back"},
        "7728": {"comment":"A separator?"},
        "7732": {"comment":"One digit placed"},
        "7735": {"synopsis":"No digit of the number reaches the places shown: the number becomes 0 (the SYS high chip's\nEXT_CLEAR_TOP), printing from digit 4, the first.","comment":"The top number := 0 through the SYS high chip"},
        "7738": {"comment":"From the first digit"},
        "7743": {"synopsis":"Works out the digits to print: B = the first digit position (4) and C = the position after\nthe last non-zero digit shown, at least the first place after the point; L = 0 when no\nfraction digit is non-zero. Positions run from 4 (the highest digit) to 15; from 16 on they\nread 0.","comment":"Keep the '^' count and the fill"},
        "7744": {"comment":"Keep B, the integer digits or exponent"},
        "7746": {"comment":"E = the integer digits less one"},
        "7748": {"comment":"C = the first fraction digit's position"},
        "7754": {"comment":"A = the integer digits"},
        "7756": {"comment":"H = the places after the point"},
        "7760": {"comment":"The last digit shown, past the first"},
        "7761": {"comment":"None reaches the places: print 0"},
        "7764": {"comment":"Below 1?"},
        "7767": {"comment":"Yes: the places after the point, from 4"},
        "7770": {"synopsis":"B = the position after the last digit shown, and L the same (non-zero), then the search\ndown."},
        "7773": {"comment":"L non-zero: not all zero yet"},
        "7774": {"synopsis":"From the last position shown down: the first non-zero digit sets C past it; all zero down to\nC gives L = 0. The JP NC (never taken: carry is set) hides LD C,B / INC C at $1E72, where a\nnon-zero digit enters.","comment":"One position down"},
        "7775": {"comment":"Beyond the 12 digits?"},
        "7778": {"comment":"Those read 0"},
        "7780": {"comment":"The digit (the SYS high chip's GET_DIGIT_EXT)"},
        "7783": {"comment":"Non-zero: the last one to print"},
        "7786": {"comment":"Down to C yet?"},
        "7791": {"comment":"All zero: L = 0"},
        "7793": {"comment":"Never taken: hides LD C,B / INC C, entry $1E72"},
        "7796": {"comment":"Print from the first digit"},
        "7798": {"synopsis":"Prints the integer part: from DE' up to the point, a ',' as it is and each place a digit,\nthe next one from position B.","comment":"At the point?"},
        "7807": {"comment":"The next field character"},
        "7810": {"comment":"A separator: print it as it is"},
        "7814": {"comment":"Beyond the 12 digits?"},
        "7819": {"comment":"The digit (the SYS high chip's GET_DIGIT_EXT)"},
        "7822": {"comment":"As a character"},
        "7824": {"comment":"The next position"},
        "7825": {"synopsis":"Prints A and goes on with the next place.","comment":"Print it"},
        "7830": {"synopsis":"At the point's place: a '.' is printed, with the ','s after it; then the fraction places.","comment":"The field's point?"},
        "7833": {"comment":"No point: the end or the exponent"},
        "7835": {"synopsis":"Prints A and goes on with the next field character after it.","comment":"Print it"},
        "7839": {"comment":"A separator next?"},
        "7845": {"comment":"An exponent field?"},
        "7849": {"comment":"Leading zeros of a number below 1 left?"},
        "7856": {"comment":"Yes: print a 0"},
        "7861": {"synopsis":"One fraction place: '#' prints the next digit, '*' and '%' a digit up to the last non-zero\none and then spaces (the first place a 0 when all are zero); any other character ends the\ndigits.","comment":"The field character"},
        "7863": {"comment":"'*'?"},
        "7867": {"comment":"'%'?"},
        "7871": {"comment":"'#'?"},
        "7873": {"comment":"No: the digits end"},
        "7878": {"synopsis":"A '*' or '%' place: before C a digit; at C a 0 when the fraction is all zero; after it a\nspace.","comment":"Before the last non-zero digit?"},
        "7881": {"comment":"Yes: print the digit"},
        "7883": {"comment":"At C with an all-zero fraction?"},
        "7886": {"comment":"$F0 + '0' gives a space"},
        "7890": {"synopsis":"Reads digit B (0 from position 16 on).","comment":"Beyond the 12 digits?"},
        "7895": {"comment":"The digit (the SYS high chip's GET_DIGIT_EXT)"},
        "7898": {"synopsis":"Moves to the next digit position and prints A as a digit.","comment":"The next position"},
        "7899": {"synopsis":"Prints A + '0'."},
        "7900": {"comment":"As a character"},
        "7904": {"synopsis":"The digits end: a '^' prints the exponent, any other character ends the field.","comment":"An exponent?"},
        "7908": {"comment":"The kept B (exponent) and D ('^' count)"},
        "7911": {"comment":"No: the field is done"},
        "7913": {"comment":"The number 0?"},
        "7919": {"comment":"Yes: exponent 0"},
        "7920": {"synopsis":"Prints the exponent: 'E', its sign, a 0 for each '^' past four, and two digits.","comment":"'E'"},
        "7925": {"comment":"Negative?"},
        "7927": {"comment":"No: '+'"},
        "7931": {"comment":"Its magnitude"},
        "7935": {"comment":"'-'"},
        "7937": {"synopsis":"Prints the exponent's sign.","comment":"Print the sign"},
        "7940": {"synopsis":"A 0 for each '^' past the fourth, passing over it in the field.","comment":"One '^' less"},
        "7942": {"comment":"Past the fourth?"},
        "7946": {"comment":"A leading 0"},
        "7952": {"comment":"Over that '^'"},
        "7956": {"synopsis":"Prints the exponent's two digits and passes over the four '^'.","comment":"The exponent"},
        "7957": {"comment":"B = 10, C = -1"},
        "7960": {"synopsis":"Counts the tens in C.","comment":"Take 10 off"},
        "7962": {"comment":"Until it goes below 0"},
        "7964": {"comment":"B = the units"},
        "7966": {"comment":"The tens digit"},
        "7972": {"comment":"The units digit"},
        "7979": {"comment":"Over the four '^'"},
        "7984": {"synopsis":"Leaves the format pointer ($172E) after the field, gives back BC', DE', HL' and goes to the\nSYS high chip's $E67A, which drops the number and marks the item printed."},
        "7985": {"comment":"$172E = after the field"},
        "7989": {"comment":"The interpreter's HL', DE', BC' back"},
        "7993": {"comment":"Back to the SYS high chip's $E67A"},
        "7999": {"synopsis":"The eleven characters of a PRINT USING number field, \"+-$<>*%#,^.\", searched by USING_SCAN\n(CPIR over 11 bytes); USING_JUMPS holds their handlers in the reverse order. ',' is not\namong the SYS high chip's USING_CHARS: before a field it is plain text, inside one a\nseparator."},
        "8010": {"synopsis":"The handlers of USING_FIELD_CHR, indexed by what CPIR leaves in C (so the last character's\nfirst): '.' UN_POINT, '^' UN_CARET, ',' USING_SCAN (nothing to count), '#' UN_HASH, '%' and\n'*' UN_FILL, '>' and '<' UN_ALIGN, '$' UN_DOLLAR, '-' $1CEC (inside UN_PLUS's JP C), '+'\nUN_PLUS."},
        "8032": {"synopsis":"Sets the fill character to '0' and falls into USING_SIGNS: the sign printed right before a\nnumber's leading 0.","comment":"Fill with '0' from here"},
        "8034": {"synopsis":"Prints a number's prefix by the flags in C: '$' when bit 1 is set, then the sign: '-' for a\nnegative number (bit 0), a space for a positive one when '-' was given (bit 7), '+' when '+'\nwas given (bit 6), else nothing.\nEntry: C = the flags.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"A '$' wanted?"},
        "8041": {"comment":"Negative: '-'"},
        "8047": {"comment":"Bit 7 into carry, bit 6 into the sign"},
        "8051": {"comment":"'-' given: a space for positive"},
        "8055": {"comment":"No '+' given: nothing"},
        "8056": {"comment":"'+'"},
        "8060": {"synopsis":"Prints A spaces (none for 0).\nEntry: A = the count.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"All printed?"},
        "8063": {"comment":"A space"},
        "8071": {"synopsis":"Reads digit B of the top number through the SYS high chip's GET_DIGIT_EXT (GET_DIGIT,\nreturning into EXTH).\nEntry: B = the digit position.\nExit: A = the digit, Z when 0.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"Keep HL"},
        "8072": {"comment":"The SYS high chip's GET_DIGIT_EXT"},
        "8077": {"synopsis":"Prints the character in A through the SYS high chip's EXTH_PUT_CHAR, which returns into\nEXTH.\nEntry: A = the character.\nChanges: nothing (HL kept).","comment":"Keep HL"},
        "8078": {"comment":"The SYS high chip's EXTH_PUT_CHAR"},
        "8081": {"synopsis":"Calls the SYS address in HL through EXTH_JUMP; the SYS routine returns into EXTH by itself.","comment":"Into SYS; back here through its EXTH_RETURN"},
        "8086": {"synopsis":"Makes the top number 0 through the SYS high chip's EXT_CLEAR_TOP, which returns into EXTH.","comment":"The SYS high chip's EXT_CLEAR_TOP"},
        "8092": {"synopsis":"PRINT USING for a string: prints the top string of the IY stack in the format field at the\nformat pointer ($172E), padded with spaces. The SYS high chip's PRINT_EXPR enters here\nthrough EXTH_JUMP with USING active.\n1. The field is an optional '<' (left aligned) or '>' (right aligned), then any of '#', '%',\n   '*'; each character is one place. With neither '<' nor '>' the string is centred, the odd\n   space after it.\n2. A string longer than the field is error 4 (observed: \"####\" with \"ABCDEFG\"; \"<\" alone\n   holds one character).\n3. Prints the leading spaces here (USING_SPACES), then goes to the SYS high chip's $E64F\n   with A = the trailing spaces, which prints the string and them.\nObserved: \">####\" with \"AB\" printed 3 spaces first, \"#####\" with \"AB\" 1, \"<####\" none.\nEntry: IY = the string (length at IY+1); ($172E) = the field's first character.\nExit: ($172E) after the field; through the SYS high chip's $E64F.","comment":"The field's first character"},
        "8096": {"comment":"D = the places, E = the alignment"},
        "8099": {"comment":"'<': left aligned (E = 0)"},
        "8103": {"comment":"E = 1: centred"},
        "8104": {"comment":"'>'?"},
        "8108": {"comment":"Right aligned: E = 2"},
        "8109": {"synopsis":"Counts a place and advances the format pointer ($172E) past it.","comment":"One more place"},
        "8111": {"comment":"$172E = the next character"},
        "8114": {"synopsis":"Counts the field's '#', '%' and '*' places; any other character ends it.","comment":"The next character"},
        "8127": {"comment":"Spare places: the field less the length"},
        "8133": {"comment":"The string is longer: error 4"},
        "8136": {"comment":"Left aligned: all spaces after"},
        "8140": {"comment":"C = the spare places"},
        "8141": {"comment":"Right aligned: all before"},
        "8143": {"comment":"Centred: half before"},
        "8145": {"synopsis":"A = the spaces after the string, C those before.","comment":"The rest after"},
        "8146": {"synopsis":"Prints the spaces before the string (none when left aligned: the sign flag from DEC E), then\nhas the SYS high chip's $E64F print the string and A spaces after it.","comment":"Keep the spaces after"},
        "8148": {"comment":"The spaces before, unless left aligned"},
        "8152": {"comment":"The SYS high chip's $E64F prints the string"},
        "8158": {"synopsis":"The text \"(C)1985ISL\" (10 bytes, no end marker); no code in the three chips reads it."},
        "8168": {"synopsis":"Calls RS232_SET_BAUD (offset $129C) with A = 4; the boot calls it at $10FF. RS232_SET_BAUD\nkeeps A in $0B69 and programs the sound generator (ports 04h-06h) from the table at\nRS232_BAUD_TABLE.","comment":"A = 4"},
        "8173": {"synopsis":"Three $00 bytes; nothing reads them."},
        "8176": {"synopsis":"Jumps to the SYS address in HL with SYS paged in: writes $70 to $0003 (the copy of port 02h)\nand port 02h (SYS in page 3), then JP (HL). EXTH's only way into the SYS chips; the SYS high\nchip's $FFF0 is the way back. The boot calls it to return to the SYS low chip's\nBOOT_IO_INIT.\nEntry: HL = the SYS address.\nChanges: nothing (AF kept).","comment":"Keep AF"},
        "8177": {"comment":"Port 02h: SYS in page 3"},
        "8179": {"comment":"Its copy at $0003"},
        "8185": {"synopsis":"JP (HL): EXTH's routines CALL it to call the address in HL (from $1123, $11CF, $1238, $125F,\n$127C); EXTH_TO_SYS ends in it.","comment":"To the address in HL"},
        "8186": {"synopsis":"Six bytes ($7B $E6 $1F $1B $FE $04) after EXTH_TO_SYS: nothing jumps to or reads them, and\nthe code before ends in JP (HL). Unused."}
      }
    }
